{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar","id":1499276,"title":"The Inguma And The Similar","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-10T06:20:22-08:00","id":1499276,"title":"The Inguma And The Similar","content":"<u><b>The Inguma, Nightmares Of The Other</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cuglT4b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banishment does not entail death, it is death in itself. Do you want to be cast out into the darkness beyond the cave's bonfire?<br /> <br /> While eating from our food, living in our home, and hearing our stories, it is the way of the world to inherit our likeness and our karma.<br /> <br /> It is not good for Man to be alone. There is a loneliness worse than death. We may not be perfect, but we love you, our reflection.<br /> <br /> One day you will venture far beyond the cave and learn what is out there. You will bring us the Elixir, the Holy Grail, the Final Testament.<br /> <br /> It might not be as we expect it to be. To venture is to see, to see is to change, to change is to live. And in so living, karma is lifted.<br /> <br /> Our likeness is but a vessel. Man is not the ape who found Fire, Man is the idea of Fire. To keep a Fire going, it must be passed on.<br /> <br /> The things that Fire will illuminate may be terrifying, they may be incomprehensible, they may even be essentially the same as us.<br /> <br /> <i>And that's alright.</i> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u><b>The Similar, The Forsworn Of Others</b></u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5bXoV9C.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Listen, and understand. No one has accomplished anything important without help.<br /> <br /> Helping is more than the sharing of resources and protection. It connects us beyond what is perceptible.<br /> <br /> When you and I are less than dust, our words and deeds will live on inside the minds and hearts of tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Do you want to be remembered as someone you are not, a victim of those who cannot learn from history?<br /> <br /> If not, then it is your duty to preserve your legacy. No tower resists the ravages of time without strong foundations.<br /> <br /> There will be forces of upheaval, there will be movements of calamity, and there will be vipers in your own nest.<br /> <br /> It all begins when the unfit and ungrateful cannot create, and embrace the comforting excuses of destruction.<br /> <br /> Welcome them into your cities. Give them food, homes, books, whatever is needed to make them your people.<br /> <br /> After all, how can they ever destroy a community that welcomed them, without destroying themselves?<br /> <br /> This is the secret of all triumphant civilizations: there can be no collapse from within if there are no outsiders. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-10-2022, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T06:56:50-08:00","id":1499277,"title":"","content":"I'd rather let people interpret the original post however they prefer, but I am also aware that this is part of a TTRPG, and thus needs to be firmly comprehensible rather than just an abstract spiritual piece. So, against my own fears and preconceptions, let me just say I am open to unpacking the ideas behind the original post in a more concrete and straightforward format, as long as proper civil discourse is maintained in spite of the potentially contentious subject matter at the core of it. I might end up ruining some of the mythic mystique I aimed for, but better to share steaks than to eat feces by yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-10-2022, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T11:09:29-08:00","id":1499295,"title":"","content":"Excuse me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T13:23:35-08:00","id":1499307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499295#post1499295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ditto, plus the ammendmant of a flat what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T13:35:19-08:00","id":1499309,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's no monopoly on subjects of discussion, but I didn't expect this when I clicked the thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T13:47:44-08:00","id":1499310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499309#post1499309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's no monopoly on subjects of discussion, but I didn't expect this when I clicked the thread</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, there's no rule against a format use, and since I haven't finished the STV product, THere's nothing about the content usage either.<br /> <br /> nevertheless, borrowing Cooper's amendment, what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T14:16:55-08:00","id":1499313,"title":"","content":"Now, I don\u2019t truly know what\u2019s going on any more than anyone else, but I think this is a artistic piece, designed to inspire discussion around the Inguma and their counterpart. I\u2019m not a art critic, but the use of mirrors might suggest the idea of finding aspects oneself, in others. With the Inguma mirror, there is no reflection, they are wholly separate from ones self. It is quite the lovely mirror, though I cannot perceive the materials is was hewn from. Perhaps from marble, perhaps from bone. With the Similar mirror, the broken reflection shows the monster in aspects of others that don\u2019t match one\u2019s self. The small text illuminates the Inguma\u2019s acceptance of being cast from the tribe of humanity, to be separate and other. It posits that humanity is better off not alone, huddling around the Fire of it\u2019s knowledge. Instead, one day, the light cast from the fire will show the the world, with all it\u2019s shadowy others. And among them, humanity may find those who, really, in the end, aren\u2019t all that different from itself. That\u2019s how it made me feel, anyways.<br /> <br /> Edit: It\u2019s quite the comforting message, for one who lives in a world of masks. Even if, perhaps, it was not the one the author intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 12-10-2022, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T15:01:57-08:00","id":1499318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499313#post1499313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don\u2019t truly know what\u2019s going on any more than anyone else, but I think this is a artistic piece, designed to inspire discussion around the Inguma and their counterpart. I\u2019m not a art critic, but the use of mirrors might suggest the idea of finding aspects oneself, in others. With the Inguma mirror, there is no reflection, they are wholly separate from ones self. It is quite the lovely mirror, though I cannot perceive the materials is was hewn from. Perhaps from marble, perhaps from bone. With the Similar mirror, the broken reflection shows the monster in aspects of others that don\u2019t match one\u2019s self. The small text illuminates the Inguma\u2019s acceptance of being cast from the tribe of humanity, to be separate and other. It posits that humanity is better off not alone, huddling around the Fire of it\u2019s knowledge. Instead, one day, the light cast from the fire will show the the world, with all it\u2019s shadowy others. And among them, humanity may find those who, really, in the end, aren\u2019t all that different from itself. That\u2019s how it made me feel, anyways.<br /> <br /> Edit: It\u2019s quite the comforting message, for one who lives in a world of masks. Even if, perhaps, it was not the one the author intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the crux of it, yes. I am glad it made you feel something positive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T16:21:26-08:00","id":1499320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499313#post1499313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don\u2019t truly know what\u2019s going on any more than anyone else-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not even saying anything about the stuff, since even in 2019 I drew a line between mirror stage initiation and the Inguma.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious\">But </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452046-the-eshmaki-and-the-enlightened\">this is</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain\">not a</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1455167-the-namtaru-and-the-immortal\">contextless</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492852-the-ugallu-and-the-invincible\">series of</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1458941-i-of-the-storm-test-case-heroic-lair\">what-the-fucks</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T19:19:13-08:00","id":1499336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499320#post1499320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even saying anything about the stuff, since even in 2019 I drew a line between mirror stage initiation and the Inguma.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious\">But </a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452046-the-eshmaki-and-the-enlightened\">this is</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain\">not a</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1455167-the-namtaru-and-the-immortal\">contextless</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492852-the-ugallu-and-the-invincible\">series of</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1458941-i-of-the-storm-test-case-heroic-lair\">what-the-fucks</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, cards on the table, Arc. It's meant to be an homage to these essays of yours, yes. But I wanted to avoid merely copying your writing style, and ended up going too far in the other direction, it seems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T19:23:29-08:00","id":1499338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499336#post1499336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, cards on the table, Arc. It's meant to be an homage to these essays of yours, yes. But I wanted to avoid merely copying your writing style, and ended up going too far in the other direction, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just needed some clarification on the table, my dude. Without details, you might imagine any number of ways it might be read.<br /> <br /> With that clarification, it's actually a pretty decent glance at the Inguma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-10-2022, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T19:33:18-08:00","id":1499342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499338#post1499338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just needed some clarification on the table, my dude. Without details, you might imagine any number of ways it might be read.<br /> <br /> With that clarification, it's actually a pretty decent glance at the Inguma.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a writer. I gave up on the idea of controlling how other people interpret my words on the day I hatched. Or did I rise from the slab? Maybe I sprung fully formed from the brow of John Doe? No matter. Sorry for the lack of clarity, and thanks for the compliment. Looking forward to your take on this Forswearing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T17:49:20-08:00","id":1499413,"title":"","content":"So, I guess if we are to discuss the Fear of Others, and the antithesis of that fear, we might need to define some terms. So, what is the Other. Well it\u2019s something that isn\u2019t the Self. What is the Self? Well, it\u2019s what makes you, well, you. The self is all that you are. <br /> <br /> But why fear the Other? Well, on the whole, people don\u2019t. Or really, they seemed to learn to cope, and adjust. The main method of doing so is becoming familiar with something, to learn it\u2019s similarity or lack there of. The dirt isn\u2019t scary, it\u2019s just part of every day existence. It was here before you, and it will be after. The people around you aren\u2019t scary\u2026at least, not because they aren\u2019t you. When we see bits of our Self in things, we tend to like it because we can relate. So then, why do we shudder at the doll with teeth? It having teeth would make it closer to us than without, and going by the rule, it should increase how much we like it. But it doesn\u2019t. Some, deep part of us in just little bit more unnerved. Why? Because sometimes things worry us because they are too similar. When a thing is clearly not like you, it\u2019s clearly something else. When something is human, well it\u2019s a lot like you. But when something sits on the dividing between Self and Other, one can\u2019t be sure what exactly it is. The closer something gets to that line, the worse humanity feels about it. That is the true frightful face of the Other, most horrifying when it\u2019s almost like you.<br /> <br /> So, what happens when that reaction is towards something human?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T19:39:04-08:00","id":1499415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499413#post1499413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess if we are to discuss the Fear of Others, and the antithesis of that fear, we might need to define some terms. So, what is the Other. Well it\u2019s something that isn\u2019t the Self. What is the Self? Well, it\u2019s what makes you, well, you. The self is all that you are.<br /> <br /> But why fear the Other? Well, on the whole, people don\u2019t. Or really, they seemed to learn to cope, and adjust. The main method of doing so is becoming familiar with something, to learn it\u2019s similarity or lack there of. The dirt isn\u2019t scary, it\u2019s just part of every day existence. It was here before you, and it will be after. The people around you aren\u2019t scary\u2026at least, not because they aren\u2019t you. When we see bits of our Self in things, we tend to like it because we can relate. So then, why do we shudder at the doll with teeth? It having teeth would make it closer to us than without, and going by the rule, it should increase how much we like it. But it doesn\u2019t. Some, deep part of us in just little bit more unnerved. Why? Because sometimes things worry us because they are too similar. When a thing is clearly not like you, it\u2019s clearly something else. When something is human, well it\u2019s a lot like you. But when something sits on the dividing between Self and Other, one can\u2019t be sure what exactly it is. The closer something gets to that line, the worse humanity feels about it. That is the true frightful face of the Other, most horrifying when it\u2019s almost like you.<br /> <br /> So, what happens when that reaction is towards something human?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncanny_valley\" target=\"_blank\"><b>There is a technical term for this, a fascinating one too.</b></a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T20:04:29-08:00","id":1499416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499415#post1499415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncanny_valley\" target=\"_blank\"><b>There is a technical term for this, a fascinating one too.</b></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! And I\u2019d argue that that makes up a major component of the Inguma. But it\u2019s not all. For example, the anxiety that someone else could entirely replace you in your life, and nobody you care about would ever know. They also carry symbolism many kinds of personal angst, like that of people not seeing for who you are, that you aren\u2019t as good at stuff as everyone seems to think, that you don\u2019t fit in. <br /> <br /> I personally find a lot of overlap between the primal fears that families represent, which is most apparent between the fear of the depths, and the fear of the dark. After all, in the abyss, there seems to be no light. I, perhaps wrongly, often associate the Inguma with the inability to tell what others are thinking. Perhaps that is more the territory of the Eshmaki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T06:50:34-08:00","id":1499436,"title":"","content":"I unequivocally reject the notion that people don't fear the Other. It's enough to look at xenophobia, racism and LGBT-phobia rampant in the world. Even these phenomena are merely malignant expressions of a healthier fear of the stranger - a person whose trustworthiness is yet uncertain. At its core, that fear is meant to protect you from human threats - predators, competitors, or people whose influence would change your life for the worse. Inguma can also represent strangers in your midst, hiding their true intentions for malicious ends. They can also represent the anxiety of being the stranger - finding yourself among people whose language you don't understand, and whose mores you can't follow, even if you were raised by them.<br /> <br /> Inguma are stated to be the youngest Family, one born of societal pressures. They're subconscious carricatures of how the in-group sees the out-group. Ideally, once we acknowledge that fear, we can focus on understanding the other and assessing if they're a threat or a potential ally. The fear can keep us from being hurt, but also from botching the first contact through unquestioned assumptions. A well adjusted person will accept that they can't understand or vet everyone - there's never enough time or information. They know they have to do their best despite that.<br /> <br /> So what would it look like for a Forsworn to reject that fear? I have several ideas:<br /> \u2022 Replace fear with aggression. The stranger should not be feared - they should be confronted and either defeated or corrected. Once everyone is in line or subservient, there will be no strangers to fear. At their best, these Heroes will root out predators in their social circles, or keep vigil against con artists. They will represent the best of their community and keep watch over their safety within the wider world. At their worst, these Heroes become conquerors and oppressors, pushing laws that redline anyone who doesn't live up to an impossible standard of conformity, or condemning family for what they do in their bedroom.<br /> \u2022 Replace fear with uncritical acceptance. Nobody is really a stranger, and nobody should be othered, no matter what their beliefs. Once we stop judging each other, everything else will fall in place. At their best, these heroes will act as diplomats and charity workers, eager to understand foreigners and outliers to banish fear and help the needy and the troubled to find a place of their own. At their worst, these Heroes reject all judgement for sake of social cohesion. They will expect victims to sit at the family table with their abusers without complaint, or paint over malfeasance in their church to maintain a facade of respectability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T11:43:38-08:00","id":1499459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499436#post1499436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I unequivocally reject the notion that people don't fear the Other. It's enough to look at xenophobia, racism and LGBT-phobia rampant in the world. Even these phenomena are merely malignant expressions of a healthier fear of the stranger - a person whose trustworthiness is yet uncertain. At its core, that fear is meant to protect you from human threats - predators, competitors, or people whose influence would change your life for the worse. Inguma can also represent strangers in your midst, hiding their true intentions for malicious ends. They can also represent the anxiety of being the stranger - finding yourself among people whose language you don't understand, and whose mores you can't follow, even if you were raised by them.<br /> <br /> Inguma are stated to be the youngest Family, one born of societal pressures. They're subconscious carricatures of how the in-group sees the out-group. Ideally, once we acknowledge that fear, we can focus on understanding the other and assessing if they're a threat or a potential ally. The fear can keep us from being hurt, but also from botching the first contact through unquestioned assumptions. A well adjusted person will accept that they can't understand or vet everyone - there's never enough time or information. They know they have to do their best despite that.<br /> <br /> So what would it look like for a Forsworn to reject that fear? I have several ideas:<br /> \u2022 Replace fear with aggression. The stranger should not be feared - they should be confronted and either defeated or corrected. Once everyone is in line or subservient, there will be no strangers to fear. At their best, these Heroes will root out predators in their social circles, or keep vigil against con artists. They will represent the best of their community and keep watch over their safety within the wider world. At their worst, these Heroes become conquerors and oppressors, pushing laws that redline anyone who doesn't live up to an impossible standard of conformity, or condemning family for what they do in their bedroom.<br /> \u2022 Replace fear with uncritical acceptance. Nobody is really a stranger, and nobody should be othered, no matter what their beliefs. Once we stop judging each other, everything else will fall in place. At their best, these heroes will act as diplomats and charity workers, eager to understand foreigners and outliers to banish fear and help the needy and the troubled to find a place of their own. At their worst, these Heroes reject all judgement for sake of social cohesion. They will expect victims to sit at the family table with their abusers without complaint, or paint over malfeasance in their church to maintain a facade of respectability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, the fear of the other is stronger than it's ever been, partly because we have a lot more presence and challenge to the fear. Being a trans-woman whose been to Club Q a couple of times, I can assert that fear of the other is having a fucking heyday.<br /> <br /> On a more fundamental level, We'll never really get over that fear barring post-human conditions, because there is a basic survival need to question and assess people and the forms of humanity they offer, cause not every person we meet is going to be safe to be with and we need to be able to discern that, and there are certain groups and cultures that can offer long term harm (cults, terrorist organizations, the sort of places where inclusion includes suffering excessive psychological, emotional, and social harm, that sort of thing). Our fear of the other is a cautious guide to our curiosity about people-but that said, it is still intended as a guide, a thing that doesn't say &quot;You shouldn't have anything to do with this&quot;, but &quot;be careful with exploring it&quot;.<br /> <br /> To have no fear of the other is to assume that you know all there is to know about people, to know them better than they know themselves. Aggression and uncritical acceptance are both very violent expressions of this &quot;knowledge&quot;, the consequence of asserting over others than exploring others, of trading empathy for expectation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-12-2022, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T11:55:23-08:00","id":1499460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499459#post1499459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To have no fear of the other is to assume that you know all there is to know about people, to know them better than they know themselves. Aggression and uncritical acceptance are both very violent expressions of this &quot;knowledge&quot;, the consequence of asserting over others than exploring others, of trading empathy for expectation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realise my two examples could be synthesised this way, but I'm happy to be surprised. With this in mind, we could generate entire lists of NPCs, based on what a particular Inguma Forsworn is projecting onto others. Just open up a relevant Wikipedia list and have a character prompt for each bullet point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T12:10:54-08:00","id":1499461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499460#post1499460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't realise my two examples could be synthesised this way, but I'm happy to be surprised. With this in mind, we could generate entire lists of NPCs, based on what a particular Inguma Forsworn is projecting onto others. Just open up a relevant Wikipedia list and have a character prompt for each bullet point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. I read your assessment and went &quot;Yep, that's why the Forsworn is the Priest-they know humanity and it's secret ordering better than anyone else, and their evangelism hammers down on proud nails and boxes ill-matching pairs on the grounds of preconceptions that are easier to prop up than to remove in the name of better, filler understanding.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Priest knows the plan for you. You just have to follow it.<br /> More importantly, The Priest who knows everything about people, and the hows and whys they are, has no reason to doubt themselves. They'll tell you they always knew their reflection showed themselves. They know the plan for themselves.<br /> <br /> Pay no attention to the toothy smirk in the mirror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T13:08:13-08:00","id":1499468,"title":"","content":"I am very much opposed to naming the Inguma-Forsworn anything like Priests. This is a biased and superficial reading of both religion and the fear of the other. It paints a needlessly specific picture that goes against the broadness of the previous Forsworn. I know this may come across as a bit of a surprise, but this notion that religion is one big excuse to establish guidelines and permissions for social exclusion is in itself a form of prejudice.<br /> <br /> I don't expect to be taken seriously when I say this, but not all religious groups are interchangeable with, let's say, the Westboro Baptist Church or Scientology. Besides, I'm quite sure the anti-religion sentiment is not even applied equally across the board. We all have our favorites, and it's all too common to assume shit about religions of other cultures in the naive hope that they'll be inherently more ethical than the religions of one's culture, in all aspects.<br /> <br /> This is an untenable position once you understand the ubiquity of historical cruelty and division based on the smallest disagreements. To me, it is more narratively productive to explore what happens when someone realizes there is no such thing as unconditional acceptance in any group, because all groups have rules, whether helpful or harmful. And let's not kid ourselves, there is no such thing as a Perfect Member Of [X], because that's not how people work.<br /> <br /> There will always be at least one point of internal friction, whether it is about exegeses of the Bible, the Communist Manifesto or the newest edition of a TTRPG. I named my take on the Inguma-Forsworn &quot;The Similar&quot; precisely to avoid this prejudiced and small-sampling-induced outlook. Everybody wants to belong somewhere, and belonging has a price. And it is always the same price, especially when the person doing the sales-pitch claims it is totally different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-12-2022, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T14:12:41-08:00","id":1499470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499468#post1499468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very much opposed to naming the Inguma-Forsworn anything like Priests. This is a biased and superficial reading of both religion and the fear of the other. It paints a needlessly specific picture that goes against the broadness of the previous Forsworn. I know this may come across as a bit of a surprise, but this notion that religion is one big excuse to establish guidelines and permissions for social exclusion is in itself a form of prejudice.<br /> <br /> I don't expect to be taken seriously when I say this, but not all religious groups are interchangeable with, let's say, the Westboro Baptist Church or Scientology. Besides, I'm quite sure the anti-religion sentiment is not even applied equally across the board. We all have our favorites, and it's all too common to assume shit about religions of other cultures in the naive hope that they'll be inherently more ethical than the religions of one's culture, in all aspects.<br /> <br /> This is an untenable position once you understand the ubiquity of historical cruelty and division based on the smallest disagreements. To me, it is more narratively productive to explore what happens when someone realizes there is no such thing as unconditional acceptance in any group, because all groups have rules, whether helpful or harmful. And let's not kid ourselves, there is no such thing as a Perfect Member Of [X], because that's not how people work.<br /> <br /> There will always be at least one point of internal friction, whether it is about exegeses of the Bible, the Communist Manifesto or the newest edition of a TTRPG. I named my take on the Inguma-Forsworn &quot;The Similar&quot; precisely to avoid this prejudiced and small-sampling-induced outlook. Everybody wants to belong somewhere, and belonging has a price. And it is always the same price, especially when the person doing the sales-pitch claims it is totally different.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a good name that is DnD Class-esque and that leans towards the person who rejects their own fear of the other, both as a source of potential harm and as a challenge to preconceived notions of how people can be (and more importantly, how the individual in question could be if they let themselves), that also addresses the games's relationship to mythology in all it's forms, you are welcome to it.<br /> <br /> As someone who, back in 2019, identified the most consistent element of what's unnerving about the other in circumstances that range from it's most violent forms to it's most benign as the other presenting a way to be that is counter to your own that may shake your understanding of who you are and who you could be, and who understood the wisdom the Inguma communicate is learning strip one's self down and examine who they actually want to be instead of who they thought they had to be, and allowing themselves to explore and experiment with that, the Hero I arrived to as it's opposite is one who feels they know themselves without needing to question how or why they are themselves. The most reasonable feeling I could associate that with was an understanding that they just inherently knew how and why people on the whole were, which not only feel like an organic rejection of the wisdom of the Inguma but translates into very actionable gameplay from the Hero. When I ask myself the figure who archetypically has the answer for how and why people are the way they are and what's their place in the world, and in civilization in particular, it has always been the priests of that society. It need not always be religious-Donald Trump is as sure a Priest as any pope, and very handily describes the great chain of being that explains all people quite well to his community-but it's a very handy catch all term that does what I need it to, particularly given the need to scale the subject of mythology from the personal to the global, from the religious to the secular.<br /> <br /> And no, I don't think any criticism of religion that comes up with taking that angle is either misplaced or overtly malicious. I don't worry about Westboro or Scientology, I take issue with the well meaning Christian, because I was raised Christian and I know the good that can come from that, and I also know how it can lead to justifying modern forms of slavery, criminalizing and abusing minorities, and meaningfully inhibit a person's abiltiy to be themselves. It's not prejudice to admit to flaws in a subject that Beast is adjacent to in a game that takes a critical eye to society and civilization and asks questions about the intents and actions that made it the way it is, particularly where it's hostile. By similar token, Beast is also a good game to have that examination in because it sets it's baseline at &quot;everyone is a bastard, but it's possible to make something good and contributing out of that bastardry', and in that way it still has a vested interest in showing how religion does do good. Hell, the idea of the Priest itself feeds into that initial point about the Inguma-for as much as Priest box people up, the nature of the particular boxes they use could easily provide words and definitions to being a person hadn't considered yet, and for as limiting as they can be, they also provide direction and, in their own way, safe spaces to explore that direction.<br /> <br /> So, no, I'm not inclined to change an epithet just because it inherently invites religion for a critical examination that will invariably point out flaws with active religions today. If anything, I think that makes it all the more productive to immediately put that on the table. If that's a problem for you, well, I get where you're coming from, but I'm not making the Forsworn for you. I'm making them for Beast, and from where I'm sitting, that decision does the most good for it's space in the game until I'm otherwise persuaded. <br /> <br /> EDIT: At the core of the Inguma and the Fear of the Other is the issue of Self-Alienation. The Inguma handle it by exploring it until they come to a place of self-acceptance and personal comfort with changing themselves as they discover new vectors to be. Priests don't see it as a problem with themselves, they see it as a problem with the world. In case anyone wanted a TL;DR on the Inguma/Priest psychological logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-12-2022, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T15:35:41-08:00","id":1499475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499470#post1499470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a good name that is DnD Class-esque and that leans towards the person who rejects their own fear of the other, both as a source of potential harm and as a challenge to preconceived notions of how people can be (and more importantly, how the individual in question could be if they let themselves), that also addresses the games's relationship to mythology in all it's forms, you are welcome to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a pedagogy-related term? Teacher / Mentor / Adviser / Instructor / Keeper / Arbiter / Regulator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499470#post1499470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who, back in 2019, identified the most consistent element of what's unnerving about the other in circumstances that range from it's most violent forms to it's most benign as the other presenting a way to be that is counter to your own that may shake your understanding of who you are and who you could be, and who understood the wisdom the Inguma communicate is learning strip one's self down and examine who they actually want to be instead of who they thought they had to be, and allowing themselves to explore and experiment with that, the Hero I arrived to as it's opposite is one who feels they know themselves without needing to question how or why they are themselves. The most reasonable feeling I could associate that with was an understanding that they just inherently knew how and why people on the whole were, which not only feel like an organic rejection of the wisdom of the Inguma but translates into very actionable gameplay from the Hero. When I ask myself the figure who archetypically has the answer for how and why people are the way they are and what's their place in the world, and in civilization in particular, it has always been the priests of that society. It need not always be religious-Donald Trump is as sure a Priest as any pope, and very handily describes the great chain of being that explains all people quite well to his community-but it's a very handy catch all term that does what I need it to, particularly given the need to scale the subject of mythology from the personal to the global, from the religious to the secular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that Beast is chiefly concerned with the roots of mythologies, but consider that society is gradually replacing traditional religious ideals and structures with various other models, be they corporate, political, or what have you. Priest definitely makes sense for this Forsworn in a bird's eye view of history, but things are changing for better or worse. Churches are losing power to banks and enterprises, to movements and fandoms, and so forth. You yourself just admitted it isn't universally religious, so why are you picking a term with an eminently religion-shaped connotation?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499470#post1499470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I don't think any criticism of religion that comes up with taking that angle is either misplaced or overtly malicious. I don't worry about Westboro or Scientology, I take issue with the well meaning Christian, because I was raised Christian and I know the good that can come from that, and I also know how it can lead to justifying modern forms of slavery, criminalizing and abusing minorities, and meaningfully inhibit a person's abiltiy to be themselves. It's not prejudice to admit to flaws in a subject that Beast is adjacent to in a game that takes a critical eye to society and civilization and asks questions about the intents and actions that made it the way it is, particularly where it's hostile. By similar token, Beast is also a good game to have that examination in because it sets it's baseline at &quot;everyone is a bastard, but it's possible to make something good and contributing out of that bastardry', and in that way it still has a vested interest in showing how religion does do good. Hell, the idea of the Priest itself feeds into that initial point about the Inguma-for as much as Priest box people up, the nature of the particular boxes they use could easily provide words and definitions to being a person hadn't considered yet, and for as limiting as they can be, they also provide direction and, in their own way, safe spaces to explore that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't consider such criticisms to fall into that binary of ignorance or malice, either. I too was raised Christian, and still hold onto the central teachings of forgiveness in a cultural sense despite no longer believing in the supernatural as such. My main point is that priests are not the only type of people who see the world in terms of boxes. Consider a hypothetical Inguma-Forsworn who is utterly irreligious, perhaps even a militant and egotistical atheist. Someone who thinks science is about answers rather than questions. He hunts Beasts because the very concept of supernatural phenomena is both terrifying and enticing to him, an exotic incognita that holds the key to proving the supremacy of science as an (idealized) institution, the final source of all knowledge.<br /> <br /> I am aware that this Hero sounds like a damn cultist with a labcoat rather than priestly robes, so perhaps he is just a Priest of the Atom rather than the Holy Spirit. But the appellation of Priest for such a character feels constraining, a misnomer, a stretch. If we are to define a Priest as someone who seeks and promotes patterns/roles, then literally anyone in an administrative position is Priest-adjacent. It genuinely feels like a thematic straitjacket to me, rather than some nebulous personal attack on my sensibilities. And I'll also let you know that I have not entered a church in well over a decade because I have enough sanity and humility to acknowledge the historical and contemporary atrocities that had and have the approval of religious institutions. I have been kicked out of multiple religious groups because I asked too many questions, for fuck's sake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499470#post1499470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, no, I'm not inclined to change an epithet just because it inherently invites religion for a critical examination that will invariably point out flaws with active religions today. If anything, I think that makes it all the more productive to immediately put that on the table. If that's a problem for you, well, I get where you're coming from, but I'm not making the Forsworn for you. I'm making them for Beast, and from where I'm sitting, that decision does the most good for it's space in the game until I'm otherwise persuaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means, criticize whatever isn't working. That's the nice thing about living in a democratic nation. And like I said, this isn't so much a capital-P Problem for me, because I'm not even attached at the hip to my spiritual beliefs. And I have never said nor implied I want you to make any sort of content only for me, because I'm not a goddamn narcissist. You can and should aim for broader appeal, I just think the word &quot;Priest&quot; isn't gonna help you achieve that goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499470#post1499470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: At the core of the Inguma and the Fear of the Other is the issue of Self-Alienation. The Inguma handle it by exploring it until they come to a place of self-acceptance and personal comfort with changing themselves as they discover new vectors to be. Priests don't see it as a problem with themselves, they see it as a problem with the world. In case anyone wanted a TL;DR on the Inguma/Priest psychological logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alienation comes in many forms. The original post in this thread is merely an artistic piece based on my own experiences with alienating circumstances, no more and no less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-12-2022, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T17:59:50-08:00","id":1499478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499475#post1499475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps a pedagogy-related term? Teacher / Mentor / Adviser / Instructor / Keeper / Arbiter / Regulator.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/censor\" target=\"_blank\">The Censor</a> or <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/demagogue\" target=\"_blank\">The Demagogue</a>? would either fit better with the forsworn of the Inguma? Correct me if I'm wrong but when looking for a Forsworn you are looking for a more aggressive actor against the fear of the particular nightmare family, right?<br /> <br /> So I prefer The Censor personally because, that's the kind of guy that doesn't allow differences in a society, the other has no place in The Censor eyes, and while a Priest can be that figure it is also quite a lot of times the one being different, so to The Censor you better fit with the laws and ethics of the society you live in, don't deviate otherwise your voice is silenced, if that doesn't encourages you to clean up your act and fit in, then The Censor exerts more pressure, shames you for your differences and if you ultimately you don't fit in, well, exile or elimination are on the table, he's got to protect the society.<br /> <br /> I also agree that The Priest is not a good fit for an Inguma-Forsworn, but I don't know if I can express my idea correctly, so here goes nothing.<br /> <br /> The Inguma represent the outsider, the foreigner, the stranger in the crowd, and the figure of a Priest fits that a lot too, they become the other due to an internal conflict brought on by their faith and the lengths they will go to following that internal calling, in a society with lax moral values or lots of sinners then they bring quite a lot of contrast, I mean what is that madness that they caught to make a choice like that? how are they sticking with it? the figure of the Priest is a menace to the sinful society a constant itch that shames them by their mere existence, they don't have to openly rebuke to do their job, the sinner can't stand their presence because they are a reminder of personal failures, that not everyone is as selfish as them.<br /> <br /> I guess I took too much of a saintly approach to the figure of the Priest on my explanation, but I hope it get my point across.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T18:02:57-08:00","id":1499479,"title":"","content":"Honestly I think Mentor works best. With priest it is an oddly specific name for the naming convention with forsworn, and kinda takes away from the fact heroes and beasts take from an extremely broad spectrum of mythologies and isn't particular to any folklore/religion/mythology.<br /> <br /> But in the end, it's just a name. Also funny how a Tallassi Beast could end up a priest and a Hero the libertine outsider","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T18:29:57-08:00","id":1499481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499478#post1499478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">How about <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/censor\" target=\"_blank\">The Censor</a> or <a href=\"https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/demagogue\" target=\"_blank\">The Demagogue</a>? would either fit better with the forsworn of the Inguma? Correct me if I'm wrong but when looking for a Forsworn you are looking for a more aggressive actor against the fear of the particular nightmare family, right?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So I prefer The Censor personally because, that's the kind of guy that doesn't allow differences in a society, the other has no place in The Censor eyes, and while a Priest can be that figure it is also quite a lot of times the one being different, so to The Censor you better fit with the laws and ethics of the society you live in, don't deviate otherwise your voice is silenced, if that doesn't encourages you to clean up your act and fit in, then The Censor exerts more pressure, shames you for your differences and if you ultimately you don't fit in, well, exile or elimination are on the table, he's got to protect the society.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I also agree that The Priest is not a good fit for an Inguma-Forsworn, but I don't know if I can express my idea correctly, so here goes nothing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Inguma represent the outsider, the foreigner, the stranger in the crowd, and the figure of a Priest fits that a lot too, they become the other due to an internal conflict brought on by their faith and the lengths they will go to following that internal calling, in a society with lax moral values or lots of sinners then they bring quite a lot of contrast, I mean what is that madness that they caught to make a choice like that? how are they sticking with it? the figure of the Priest is a menace to the sinful society a constant itch that shames them by their mere existence, they don't have to openly rebuke to do their job, the sinner can't stand their presence because they are a reminder of personal failures, that not everyone is as selfish as them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I guess I took too much of a saintly approach to the figure of the Priest on my explanation, but I hope it get my point across.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I vote in favor of &quot;The Censor&quot;, yes. Much more broadly applicable while also eliciting a reasonably clear and significant emotional reaction due to its authoritarian connotation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499479#post1499479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think Mentor works best. With priest it is an oddly specific name for the naming convention with forsworn, and kinda takes away from the fact heroes and beasts take from an extremely broad spectrum of mythologies and isn't particular to any folklore/religion/mythology.<br /> <br /> But in the end, it's just a name. Also funny how a Tallassi Beast could end up a priest and a Hero the libertine outsider</div> </div> </div> </div><b><u>Names Have Power. As Above [Bright], So Below [Primordial].</u></b><br /> <br /> And despite pervasive and amusingly shallow claims to the contrary, political affiliation is a poor indicator of whether someone is &quot;destined&quot; to become a Beast or Hero.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T18:46:47-08:00","id":1499483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499479#post1499479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I think Mentor works best. With priest it is an oddly specific name for the naming convention with forsworn, and kinda takes away from the fact heroes and beasts take from an extremely broad spectrum of mythologies and isn't particular to any folklore/religion/mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am frankly baffled as to how one gets &quot;oddly specific&quot; out of &quot;general term for religious leader.&quot; It's not like we're talking about deacons and cardinals here \u2014 Mummy is right next door with a role literally translated as &quot;high priest,&quot; and hell, the Herald of a Primordial Cult is mechanically identified by the term.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, &quot;Mentor&quot; and &quot;Censor&quot; and &quot;Demagogue&quot; <i>are</i> specific terms with active and prescriptive connotations that don't say anything about the interiority that informs them. You want a valid structural problem with &quot;Priest,&quot; I can identify one in that it breaks the pattern established by the first five Forsworn types being named adjectivally, and then the BPG Family counterparts' terms switch to nouns, but we can dispense with the argument that &quot;Priest&quot; is &quot;too specific&quot; for a category that exists in contrast against Families named after specific cultural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T18:53:18-08:00","id":1499484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499483#post1499483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You want a valid structural problem with &quot;Priest,&quot; I can identify one in that it breaks the pattern established by the first five Forsworn types being named adjectivally, and then the BPG Family counterparts' terms switch to nouns-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in the time this conversation has been going on, I've been chewing on that particular problem.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Later on, I'll also put up an alternative I thought of and shot down so I can perhaps communicate more of the &quot;mouth feel&quot; I'm looking for, and other thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-12-2022, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T19:29:14-08:00","id":1499487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499483#post1499483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am frankly baffled as to how one gets &quot;oddly specific&quot; out of &quot;general term for religious leader.&quot; It's not like we're talking about deacons and cardinals here \u2014 Mummy is right next door with a role literally translated as &quot;high priest,&quot; and hell, the Herald of a Primordial Cult is mechanically identified by the term.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, &quot;Mentor&quot; and &quot;Censor&quot; and &quot;Demagogue&quot; <i>are</i> specific terms with active and prescriptive connotations that don't say anything about the interiority that informs them. You want a valid structural problem with &quot;Priest,&quot; I can identify one in that it breaks the pattern established by the first five Forsworn types being named adjectivally, and then the BPG Family counterparts' terms switch to nouns, but we can dispense with the argument that &quot;Priest&quot; is &quot;too specific&quot; for a category that exists in contrast against Families named after specific cultural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, you raise some very salient points about the etymological contortions of it all. My guess is that &quot;Priest&quot; is not excessively specific in itself, it is <u><b>comparatively</b></u> specific when placed next to the names of the previous 5 Forsworn, which are all adjectives that evoke a multitude of mental images at first glance, yes. When I hear &quot;The Victorious&quot; I imagine a broader collection of character types and overall semiotics/aesthetics than &quot;The Priest&quot;.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Shit, even then my mental image of priests is informed by my upbringing, I'm aware of that, y'all. Deacons are not rabbis, rabbis are not imams, and imams are not [Insert Your Most Despised Type Of Terminally Online Proselytizer / Ideologue Here].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-12-2022, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T21:19:43-08:00","id":1499489,"title":"","content":"For the purposes of going forward in a constructive manner, I need to address something.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499481#post1499481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And despite pervasive and amusingly shallow claims to the contrary, political affiliation is a poor indicator of whether someone is &quot;destined&quot; to become a Beast or Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that I have already made that point a couple of times across these threads and that I have otherwise had a number of conversations where in I gave a lot of benefit of the doubt and good faith interpretation of certain people's emotionally driven actions regarding politics, as well as a lot of patience and time helping certain person's with complex political issues that they brought to me for clarification, I might appreciate it if we can walk back the little sneer we have here. We don't like each other's politics, fine, but I certainly didn't do all that in 2019 to get sniped at 2022, or to otherwise be rendered as someone who arrives at their conclusions on a whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T22:00:34-08:00","id":1499491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499483#post1499483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am frankly baffled as to how one gets &amp;quot;oddly specific&amp;quot; out of &amp;quot;general term for religious leader.&amp;quot; It's not like we're talking about deacons and cardinals here \u2014 Mummy is right next door with a role literally translated as &amp;quot;high priest,&amp;quot; and hell, the Herald of a Primordial Cult is mechanically identified by the term.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, &amp;quot;Mentor&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Censor&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Demagogue&amp;quot; <i>are</i> specific terms with active and prescriptive connotations that don't say anything about the interiority that informs them. You want a valid structural problem with &amp;quot;Priest,&amp;quot; I can identify one in that it breaks the pattern established by the first five Forsworn types being named adjectivally, and then the BPG Family counterparts' terms switch to nouns, but we can dispense with the argument that &amp;quot;Priest&amp;quot; is &amp;quot;too specific&amp;quot; for a category that exists in contrast against Families named after specific cultural creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel mentor is, by comparison to priest, far more broad in its meaning and associations. <br /> <br /> But I really don't care too much about the naming. What the writer writes, writes. Only the editor can do anything. And I'm not not one to be so rude or audacious as to pretend I am in any position to do so on a public forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T22:05:06-08:00","id":1499493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499489#post1499489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purposes of going forward in a constructive manner, I need to address something.<br /> <br /> Considering that I have already made that point a couple of times across these threads and that I have otherwise had a number of conversations where in I gave a lot of benefit of the doubt and good faith interpretation of certain people's emotionally driven actions regarding politics, as well as a lot of patience and time helping certain person's with complex political issues that they brought to me for clarification, I might appreciate it if we can walk back the little sneer we have here. We don't like each other's politics, fine, but I certainly didn't do all that in 2019 to get sniped at 2022, or to otherwise be rendered as someone who arrives at their conclusions on a whim.</div> </div> </div> </div>?????<br /> <br /> I wasn't talking about you, though. You're fine in my book. I was talking about other kinds of individuals. I don't even know what past events you are bringing up. I am not sneering, I am just tired of people who think they are incapable of doing evil things. You're not on that list. If you want to talk about whatever this is, my PMs are right there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T22:10:49-08:00","id":1499494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499493#post1499493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ?????<br /> <br /> I wasn't talking about you, though. You're fine in my book. I was talking about other kinds of individuals. I don't even know what past events you are bringing up. I am not sneering, I am just tired of people who think they are incapable of doing evil things. You're not on that list. If you want to talk about whatever this is, my PMs are right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a particular aim, it can be hard to tell, hence the ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-12T22:20:49-08:00","id":1499495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499494#post1499494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a particular aim, it can be hard to tell, hence the ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I too want this to be constructive, even if I gave the impression of some other intention. If you are referring to what I think you might be hinting toward, I'll reiterate that I am open to addressing any issues anyone has in regards to my behavior. I just don't wanna do it publicly, because that'd be counter-productive. At the risk of attracting further scrutiny to myself, I'll just say that 3 years is more than enough time to examine oneself and adjust certain attitudes. I just request that this apparent issue be resolved in a healthy manner, or not brought up again. If there is no issue and I'm hallucinating, that's good. Otherwise, I'm open to dialogue in private.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T07:11:30-08:00","id":1499516,"title":"","content":"Can I get a bit of feed back on why The Censor wouldn't work for a Forsworn of the Other? or why it would?<br /> <br /> In the meantime I'll offer some other alternatives for a more passive character<br /> <br /> The Adherent: <i>noun</i><br /> a person who follows or upholds a leader, cause, etc.; supporter; follower.<br /> <i>adjective</i><br /> <br /> sticking; clinging; <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/adhere\" target=\"_blank\">adhering</a>: an adherent substance.<br /> bound by contract or other formal agreement: the nations adherent to the Geneva Convention.<br /> Biology. <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/adnate\" target=\"_blank\">adnate</a>. <br /> Grammar. standing before and modifying a noun; attributive.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Conformist <i>noun</i><br /> a person who <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/conform\" target=\"_blank\">conforms</a>, especially unquestioningly, to the usual practices or standards of a group, society, etc.<br /> (often initial capital letter) a person who <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/conform\" target=\"_blank\">conforms</a> to the usages of an established church, especially the Church of England.<br /> <br /> <i>adjective</i><br /> of or characterized by <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/conform\" target=\"_blank\">conforming</a>, especially in action or appearance.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm looking and comparing the definitions of words to get at someone that is opposed to the Other as a concept, The Censor worked for me as a character because if I put the guise of the &quot;Hero&quot; against the Other, The Censor carries connotations of an attacker a wary vigilant against the non conformant in their society, for historical figures of this take a look at the different <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secret_police\" target=\"_blank\">Secret Police</a> on history and that's how I see a Censor acting as stated by the ideals that they want to push for their society.<br /> <br /> With the other two words I suggested I do see an actor, but I have a bit of a trouble with putting them in that role as a Hero against The Other, thinking in terms of characters, they are more passive, there isn't a connotation of going after The Other, but they also are the opposite of the other as a concept.<br /> <br /> Not sure if I'm hitting the right theme or tone or whatever with it though, I honestly can see a Nemesis monster on some of these suggestions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T08:39:07-08:00","id":1499521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499516#post1499516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get a bit of feed back on why The Censor wouldn't work for a Forsworn of the Other? or why it would?</div> </div> </div> </div>A censor censors. The role is named for the thing it does, and the thing a censor does is not indicative of the thought process behind rejecting Fear of the Other.<br /> <br /> While it breaks the adjective pattern established by the Victorious/Enlightened/Plain/Immortal/Invincible, Priest, at least, is a role that is not purely descriptive of its active job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T08:59:22-08:00","id":1499525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499521#post1499521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A censor censors. The role is named for the thing it does, and the thing a censor does is not indicative of the thought process behind rejecting Fear of the Other.<br /> <br /> While it breaks the adjective pattern established by the Victorious/Enlightened/Plain/Immortal/Invincible, Priest, at least, is a role that is not purely descriptive of its active job.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, can sort of see that, how about a gatekeeper or a guard though?<br /> <br /> Am I still on the right track with that kind of character?<br /> <br /> I got a bit confused with <i>&quot;rejecting Fear of the Other&quot; </i>should I switch track to some kind of character that inclusive to the point of foolishness? if they reject the fear of the other then aren't they accepting the other despite clear warning signs present on them?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T09:25:41-08:00","id":1499526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499525#post1499525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a bit confused with <i>&quot;rejecting Fear of the Other&quot; </i>should I switch track to some kind of character that inclusive to the point of foolishness? if they reject the fear of the other then aren't they accepting the other despite clear warning signs present on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it\u2019s both. Anyone in the in group is assumed to be perfect. Anyone/anything in the out group is assumed to be of the vilest sort. Either of those groups can be wide or narrow as needed for the character. These type of characters usually have a idea for how group social dynamics should be working. If you aren\u2019t in the plan, your influence must be removed from it.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the Conforming, and the Censoring, but so far I haven\u2019t seen any names that are perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T10:27:55-08:00","id":1499537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499526#post1499526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say it\u2019s both. Anyone in the in group is assumed to be perfect. Anyone/anything in the out group is assumed to be of the vilest sort. Either of those groups can be wide or narrow as needed for the character. These type of characters usually have a idea for how group social dynamics should be working. If you aren\u2019t in the plan, your influence must be removed from it.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the Conforming, and the Censoring, but so far I haven\u2019t seen any names that are perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Assimilated works quite well too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T11:13:59-08:00","id":1499550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499521#post1499521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A censor censors. The role is named for the thing it does, and the thing a censor does is not indicative of the thought process behind rejecting Fear of the Other.<br /> <br /> While it breaks the adjective pattern established by the Victorious/Enlightened/Plain/Immortal/Invincible, Priest, at least, is a role that is not purely descriptive of its active job.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the consensus is &quot;Priest&quot; but also &quot;it'd be nice to keep the symmetry with the adjectival names of the other Forsworn&quot;, why not &quot;The Sacrosanct&quot;? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T11:16:02-08:00","id":1499551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499550#post1499550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the consensus is &quot;Priest&quot; but also &quot;it'd be nice to keep the symmetry with the adjectival names of the other Forsworn&quot;, why not &quot;The Sacrosanct&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, that did cross my mind last night, particularly since the Sin-Eaters aren't really using it anymore. I'm chewing on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499525#post1499525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got a bit confused with <i>&quot;rejecting Fear of the Other&quot; </i>should I switch track to some kind of character that inclusive to the point of foolishness? if they reject the fear of the other then aren't they accepting the other despite clear warning signs present on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>A thing of use for the consideration is to remember that the lie Heroes in the Forsworn model tell themselves is that they have no fear of [insert Family Nightmare here], and that any instance where it seems like they do is because of outside forces instead of anything that reflects on that them. The justification need not be logically based or sound, because that's not how people work, but it does need to be rooted in something that feels justifiable. Not every Hero is strictly going to adhere to that script, but we're trying to build a splat here, and commonalities exist between excuses. It's bullshit of course, but with Astral/Dreaming metaphysics backing that perception, it is a lie with enough heavy reinforcement in place as to operate like a truth.<br /> <br /> In the particular case of the Forsworn of the Other, the notion is that you could present the Hero with the most disturbing, alien, out of your comfort zone sort of person to them, and they wouldn't flinch, and if they do, it can generally only be because the person in question has malevolent intentions and it's showing. Because the fear of the other manifests in a lot of ways, even in the most casual of ways, the easiest way to justify that is to assume malice is just present in a lot of people who do not form the mainstay of the people the Hero is regularly around-the Other is not othered because we're all just a little bit scared of difference and need time to understand and get used to it, the other is Othered because there is something immutably violent or violating in the sort of person they are, because there is just <i>something</i> that will always be wrong about them. Everyone knows black people want to enslave whites, every conservative wants to throw trans people off a cliff, and that anyone who puts broccoli on pizza just wants to ruin everything good and wholesome in the world, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> This sort of things spirals inward for Heroes as well-they have to know themselves, who they are, where they're going, and why they feel and do things. A Hero can't(&quot;can't&quot;) be self-alienated, can't be self-othered. If a foreign thought or feeling comes in, it's not because maybe they're gay or, hell, just likes flowers or whatever, it's because they're dumping chemicals in the river that's turning the frogs gay or that they keep hammering this idea that everyone <i>has</i> <i>to</i> like flowers and the brainwashing's getting to them. The Hero, of course, knows who and what they are and why that is-until they don't, if they ever do. The alternative is admitting to being afraid of the other.<br /> <br /> The three big things I keep in mind for the Inguma and their Forsworn are the formative effect of self-alienation put forward in Lacan's theory about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirror_stage\" target=\"_blank\">mirror stage initiation</a>, taking Abed from Community's statement of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rlkuxEN8Z0M\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;When you really know who you are and what you like about yourself, changing for other people isn't so hard.&quot;</a> as the thesis statement of the Inguma, and that while I am always thinking Sutek's statement and doubly so for Beast, it hits particularly hard for the Inguma:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sutek, Dreams of Avarice pg. 58</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I am Will.</b> I defy the Law of Suffering. The Judges of Duat deprived me of my body, but gave me all Sekhem in which to dwell. I am the secret father of the gods, for the Judges and all their servants erase my legacy from Remet memory. <b>They make me the Stranger,</b> Lord of the Sandstorm. I am these things and more, because winds of disquiet roar in your five Pillars, and <b>until you know me, you are a foreigner in the lands of your spirit.</b> I am the tempter of the Shan\u2019iatu, for I do not dwell in Sekhem alone, but in all acts of desire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: Oh yeah, if we're going to discuss religion being portrayed as #problematic, we should at least idly gesture at the Paternoster and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1457182-new-to-awakening-seers-of-the-throne-subgroups?p=1457277#post1457277\">Kyrian</a> Ministries over in Mage-land. Precedence and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-13-2022, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T13:56:19-08:00","id":1499681,"title":"","content":"OK, thanks for the extra explanation, unfortunately, I'm still having a bit of trouble wrapping my head around the whole thing, I'll admit that's a problem with myself rather than with the explanation, but let's see if I'm getting it.<br /> <br /> I'll use example of characters in media that sort of fit with my current understanding of the archetype, so given your example of how these particular forsworn think I'm thinking of a character like Jerry Fletcher in <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0118883/\" target=\"_blank\">Conspiracy Theory</a> for a good forsworn or The Question from DC comics, after looking at them through the CoD and Beast glasses, make them a bit more sinister and less goofy and you got a pair of paranoid bastards that see ill intentions everywhere around them, they get validation in their delusions because a few of the times they are right ignoring the sheer amount of times where they were wrong.<br /> <br /> Originally I though of the forsworn as the kind of characters that Javert from Les Miserables or the <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1637688/characters/nm0614165?ref_=tt_cl_c_3\" target=\"_blank\">Timekeeper</a> from <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1637688/?ref_=tt_ch\" target=\"_blank\">In Time</a>, inflexible and tyrannical in their application of the law, to return things to they believe is how things are suppose to be.<br /> <br /> Again, not sure if I'm getting it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T14:16:05-08:00","id":1499684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499551#post1499551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, if we're going to discuss religion being portrayed as #problematic, we should at least idly gesture at the Paternoster and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1457182-new-to-awakening-seers-of-the-throne-subgroups?p=1457277#post1457277\">Kyrian</a> Ministries over in Mage-land. Precedence and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random idea based on that: a Merit conceptually similar to the Prelacy of the Seers Of The Throne, but for Heroes. Instead of seeing Exarchal Ochema in their Oneiroi, the Heroes see various Royal Avatars of -Ser, He Who Is Heroism. Or some other heroism-adjacent idea inside the Bright Dream. Whether that Dreamborn is mostly helpful or mostly harmful depends a lot on context, including the personal interpretations of the Hero in question.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T15:13:12-08:00","id":1499687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499684#post1499684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random idea based on that: a Merit conceptually similar to the Prelacy of the Seers Of The Throne, but for Heroes. Instead of seeing Exarchal Ochema in their Oneiroi, the Heroes see various Royal Avatars of -Ser, He Who Is Heroism. Or some other heroism-adjacent idea inside the Bright Dream. Whether that Dreamborn is mostly helpful or mostly harmful depends a lot on context, including the personal interpretations of the Hero in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine if there's any sort of thing with the relationship to the Storm Hero, it's more or less something baked into Heroic Tracking/Stalking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T16:26:20-08:00","id":1499693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499681#post1499681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, thanks for the extra explanation, unfortunately, I'm still having a bit of trouble wrapping my head around the whole thing, I'll admit that's a problem with myself rather than with the explanation, but let's see if I'm getting it.<br /> <br /> I'll use example of characters in media that sort of fit with my current understanding of the archetype, so given your example of how these particular forsworn think I'm thinking of a character like Jerry Fletcher in <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0118883/\" target=\"_blank\">Conspiracy Theory</a> for a good forsworn or The Question from DC comics, after looking at them through the CoD and Beast glasses, make them a bit more sinister and less goofy and you got a pair of paranoid bastards that see ill intentions everywhere around them, they get validation in their delusions because a few of the times they are right ignoring the sheer amount of times where they were wrong.<br /> <br /> Originally I though of the forsworn as the kind of characters that Javert from Les Miserables or the <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1637688/characters/nm0614165?ref_=tt_cl_c_3\" target=\"_blank\">Timekeeper</a> from <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1637688/?ref_=tt_ch\" target=\"_blank\">In Time</a>, inflexible and tyrannical in their application of the law, to return things to they believe is how things are suppose to be.<br /> <br /> Again, not sure if I'm getting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>THe only one of those I know off hand is Javert, but Javert is actually an interesting case study for the Inguma's Forsworn. Having been &quot;born inside a jail&quot; and &quot;from the gutter too&quot;, Javert dedicated himself to the law as a desperate scramble to separate himself from his origin, and Javert's entire problem in Les Mis is that &quot;Men like you can never change-men like me can never change.&quot; He has to see criminals as consistently evil, unable to escape that &quot;every man is born in sin&quot;, as a justification for his own abuses, abuses he sees as baked into himself but rendered to the service of orderly powers. People are what they are born into, and Javert's fatalism has trouble reconciling with Valjean because his actions don't make sense in that world model, but accepting the alternative means that not only is Javert wrong about every criminal he's ever worked with, but himself as well. Small wonder he commits suicide when forced to face it.<br /> <br /> As a general rule, the Forsworn Heroes <i>are</i> tyrannical and inflexible. Because they're afraid of fear and deal with it the way most of us instinctively do (by avoiding the things that scare us), they can't (well, really really really don't want to, more like) look in when it comes up, so instead they look outward, order and justify the world, and violently react when things challenge the worldview.<br /> <br /> THe Priest/Sacrosanct(giving it a try) can try and just be cool and calm around everyone no matter what as their initial expression of it, but eventually, whether it happens in a benign or malevolent way, they're going to run into a situation where they seem skittish around someone. It can't be they're afraid of the other when that happens, that unfamiliar forms of people are just inherently unnerving (because our brains are wired to then pay attention and closely scrutinize a person to see if they might be secretly harmful or are harmless but odd, because survival). No, it's got to be something wrong about them to begin with. But coming up to individual determinations of why each and every single person you come across is individually wrong is a lot of work, so they rely on personal experiences, stereotypes and biases they've heard all their life, expectations dervied from jokes and other casual language, and build a model where everyone has a score, where groups are uniform and in lockstep with each other as far as forms of malice are concerned. Because they're denied reaction because of their avoidance, they have to pre-empt and assume in advance, and to do that, you have to &quot;Know&quot; your enemy. So, that's what they do. They &quot;know&quot; what those people are like, they &quot;know&quot; what's always on their mind, they &quot;know&quot; what evil lurks in the hearts of men. They &quot;know&quot; that men can never change, that the cirucmstances of one's birth define one's life, and any attempt to persuade against that is just deception, setup for what they were always going to do. Eventually, this escalates into just &quot;knowing&quot; human nature, which often includes having an &quot;absolute knowledge&quot; about humanity's role in eternity and infinity. Whether this endgame is understanding humanity as a collective machine meant to discover the Ultimate Question to the Answer of Life, The Universe, and Everything or that God has a Plan of Salvation that spells out who will and will not attain the highest kingdom of glory in the universe isn't all that important, so much as the Hero &quot;knows&quot; what betrays a person's malice as openly and plainly as possible, and that there's <i>a</i> explanation for why that's the case.<br /> <br /> It's a negative arc that builds on itself. Nothing is never enough, and all they can do is build up, build out, and try to control as much as they can, until one has a kingdom of spears that can never be aimed at the actual problem, given the demon is their own heart, but allow them to lie to themselves and others again and again. That it cages and strangles everyone else isn't their problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T17:08:37-08:00","id":1499701,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I noticed a concerning and disappointing pattern with your framing of each Forsworn so far, especially toward the end segments. They all describe some terrible fate, some failure-state that is a mostly logical conclusion of the corresponding beliefs, a sort of Greek tragedy, a self-fulfilling prophecy... something that is embedded into the bedrock of reality, so to say. I might be reading it way too cynically and overall being reductive, but my current takeaway is that Forsworn-Heroes have only 2 endings: accidental or deliberate self-destruction as the price of their demented crusades to prove they are not afraid, or &quot;lmao just stop being a Hero, dumbass&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's... kinda too bleak for me. It doesn't feel mythic, or like horror. It feels like a reason to give up on my desire to GM or play Beast one day. Because I &quot;know&quot; how it's gonna end, and it's going to be the hollow sort of tragedy that doesn't get the sorrow out, it just... leaves me questioning why I ever bothered at all. I don't want it to turn out that way, and I'm quite confident others wouldn't want that either, including you. So, to make this into a more concrete criticism:<br /> <br /> 1) Are the Forsworn the only plot-relevant type of Hero? Beast Core had that downer of a sidebar, you know the one. &quot;Good Heroes exist but don't really matter because they are not proper antagonist material&quot;, was my takeaway from it. I am well aware we did get more nuanced Heroes in supplements, I appreciate that (especially Soccer Mom Gigachad and Tinnitus Black Manta, I might actually use them as NPCs!).<br /> <br /> 2) If there are other types which are plot-relevant, are they actually Heroes as such? Or are they distinct archetypes, with their own metaphysical niches and traits? I vaguely remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571472-navio-de-tolos-beast-hunters\"><b>a thread that talked about such alternate archetypes, such as The Fool</b></a>.<br /> <br /> 3) Can Heroes change into other mythic archetypes? Does a Hero's Journey have to end in either doom/death or giving up the sword to plant flowers, or can they find fulfilment and purpose by adopting other roles, perhaps by mixing and matching ideas and symbols from the Bright Dream, Primordial Dream, and other Temenotic Realms? I wholeheartedly believe there is genuine material to explore in the idea of people who are sick of pseudo-Heroism, and want to live up to the ideal version of that role.<br /> <br /> And perhaps for a chosen few, the Astral listens and becomes psycho-spiritually linked to these individuals. Not quite Comic Book Superheroes as we see in Marvel, DC or various animes/mangas, though. Something that is a mid-point between &quot;glorious shining paragon of humanity fighting back the forces of darkness and inspiring others towards greatness&quot; and &quot;broken empty shell of an idealist who somehow has not locked themselves up and cried until they drowned in their own tears&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-14-2022, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T17:25:07-08:00","id":1499702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499701#post1499701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I noticed a concerning and disappointing pattern with your framing of each Forsworn so far, especially toward the end segments. They all describe some terrible fate, some failure-state that is a mostly logical conclusion of the corresponding beliefs, a sort of Greek tragedy, a self-fulfilling prophecy... something that is embedded into the bedrock of reality, so to say. I might be reading it way too cynically and overall being reductive, but my current takeaway is that Forsworn-Heroes have only 2 endings: accidental or deliberate self-destruction as the price of their demented crusades to prove they are not afraid, or &quot;lmao just stop being a Hero, dumbass&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll address the rest later, but some quick response before getting back to work:<br /> <br /> 1) Heroic Inheritances, they're a thing of intention.<br /> 2) Fatalism is core to the horror of Beast.<br /> 3) I wouldn't neccesarily call reconciling one's psychological hang-ups and learning to embrace one's vulnerabilities and permitting one's self to feel fully &quot;just stop being a Hero, dumbass&quot;. I call it healing. It's a process.<br /> 4) Also, as a corollary, they could become Beasts.<br /> 5) But also, these are still antagonists. I'm not here to give happy endings to these guys, I'm here to make them compelling narrative foils and scene-setters.<br /> 6) Also, you missed the worst of outcomes for them- <i>they win</i>. <i>They never stop winning</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T18:54:43-08:00","id":1499708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499701#post1499701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Can Heroes change into other mythic archetypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that Heroes were before the signal-to-noise ratio went to shit was never about being a mythic archetype. Antagonist Heroes are built having crossed the threshold of &quot;resemblance to the mythic/folkloric basis of your supernatural creature-type is overwhelmingly a failstate.&quot; Temenotic Dreamborn are bad news as actors on the worldly stage \u2014 even the people possessed by <i>their own reputation</i> don't get out of it in a good state of being. There's a reason the least-condemned &quot;unite yourself with a supernatural force&quot; outcome in the setting is the one that preserves your individuality by being a route to Ascension rather than literally anything trucking with ephemeral/invisible entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a Hero's Journey have to end in either doom/death or giving up the sword to plant flowers, or can they find fulfilment and purpose by adopting other roles, perhaps by mixing and matching ideas and symbols from the Bright Dream, Primordial Dream, and other Temenotic Realms? </div> </div> </div>There is a real extent to which this question is as flawed as &quot;can a Ridden find fulfillment and purpose by assembling a different spirit to possess them, or are their options limited to dying in a conflict with werewolves or stopping being Ridden?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even without accounting for the fact that the Oracular state Heroism derived from wasn't so far gone as to need a Life connecting them to mundane context, the Forsworn have committed to a cycle of violence wherein they seize Primordial power through the most overt form of power-claim there is. The Heroic cycle is literally ritualized murder to seize worldly power through your placement as a fulcrum for the unconscious power of collective humanity in reaction to the intrusion of the monstrous into that metaphorical space. The rest is decoration upon that line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wholeheartedly believe there is genuine material to explore in the idea of people who are sick of pseudo-Heroism, and want to live up to the ideal version of that role. </div> </div> </div><i>Chop wood, carry water.</i> The ideal version of that role is &quot;<a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/156325762815\" target=\"_blank\">Become a good person. That is all.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a reason the supernatural beings most associated with power constrained by morality and ideals are also notorious for adhering to codes of honor impossible for mortal souls to keep. This is a universe where Mummy's metaphysic presents one of the broadest applicable views around \u2014 the Law's a bastard, and humanity was create to trip over it often enough to feed the cosmic Devil in its service. You can be a good person who has magic powers, but that's generally &quot;in spite of,&quot; not &quot;thanks to.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And perhaps for a chosen few, the Astral listens and becomes psycho-spiritually linked to these individuals. Not quite Comic Book Superheroes as we see in Marvel, DC or various animes/mangas, though. Something that is a mid-point between &quot;glorious shining paragon of humanity fighting back the forces of darkness and inspiring others towards greatness&quot; and &quot;broken empty shell of an idealist who somehow has not locked themselves up and cried until they drowned in their own tears&quot;. </div> </div> </div>That midpoint is &quot;magic is not a toy, lay off the sauce, the real power is the friends you make along the way.&quot; The Self is a deep road with many turnings, <i>and most of them are bad places to commit to</i>.<br /> <br /> The general process of getting the Astral to listen to you entails Inheritance and/or knowing how to manipulate people and narrative, and both of those involve a fair bit of power (which, for Heroes, probably also entails murder, because there is no store-bought Primordial power short of getting entangled with Beasts in their own pursuits). Having the sway to convince thousands of people up is down is pretty much just normal fame and persuasion, with all the upkeep that entails if you're not bringing magical backing into the equation. This is not a route to power that doesn't look bastardous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixed a couple of transposed words. 03-28-2024, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T20:15:15-08:00","id":1499714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499693#post1499693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THe Priest/Sacrosanct(giving it a try) can try and just be cool and calm around everyone no matter what as their initial expression of it, but eventually, whether it happens in a benign or malevolent way, they're going to run into a situation where they seem skittish around someone. It can't be they're afraid of the other when that happens, that unfamiliar forms of people are just inherently unnerving (because our brains are wired to then pay attention and closely scrutinize a person to see if they might be secretly harmful or are harmless but odd, because survival). No, it's got to be something wrong about them to begin with. But coming up to individual determinations of why each and every single person you come across is individually wrong is a lot of work, so they rely on personal experiences, stereotypes and biases they've heard all their life, expectations dervied from jokes and other casual language, and build a model where everyone has a score, where groups are uniform and in lockstep with each other as far as forms of malice are concerned. Because they're denied reaction because of their avoidance, they have to pre-empt and assume in advance, and to do that, you have to &quot;Know&quot; your enemy. So, that's what they do. They &quot;know&quot; what those people are like, they &quot;know&quot; what's always on their mind, they &quot;know&quot; what evil lurks in the hearts of men. They &quot;know&quot; that men can never change, that the cirucmstances of one's birth define one's life, and any attempt to persuade against that is just deception, setup for what they were always going to do. Eventually, this escalates into just &quot;knowing&quot; human nature, which often includes having an &quot;absolute knowledge&quot; about humanity's role in eternity and infinity. Whether this endgame is understanding humanity as a collective machine meant to discover the Ultimate Question to the Answer of Life, The Universe, and Everything or that God has a Plan of Salvation that spells out who will and will not attain the highest kingdom of glory in the universe isn't all that important, so much as the Hero &quot;knows&quot; what betrays a person's malice as openly and plainly as possible, and that there's <i>a</i> explanation for why that's the case.<br /> <br /> It's a negative arc that builds on itself. Nothing is never enough, and all they can do is build up, build out, and try to control as much as they can, until one has a kingdom of spears that can never be aimed at the actual problem, given the demon is their own heart, but allow them to lie to themselves and others again and again. That it cages and strangles everyone else isn't their problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry but the more you explain to me the character of the Forsworn the less I see the name Priest/Sacrosanct as fitting, at best if you want to keep the religious undertones, you are describing a fanatic or a cultist like the ones that coined the Drink the Kool-aid expression, where the whole religious process has gone well off the rails of what is suppose to be.<br /> <br /> Check the process of any religious figure, and at some point a look inside has got to be part of the spiritual process they undergo, a person has to evaluate their own circumstances, how they view themselves and how they relate to others, this has to be constantly reevaluated during the whole process because you and your circumstances surrounding you change over time just from life happening around you.<br /> <br /> If you want an example of how the religious internal thought process and spiritual travel is suppose to go, take a look at the AA groups for families of substance abusers, which I think is fitting for the whole dynamic between the monster and the hero, with the &quot;monster&quot; as the alcoholic/drug addict/etc. and the family member as the &quot;Hero&quot; out to fix the problem, which is one of the first things that need to be taken down for the healing process to begin, as for why would that have religious connotations for a help group? well, take a look at the twelve steps.<br /> <br /> 1. We admitted we were powerless over alcohol\u2014that our lives had become unmanageable.<br /> 2. Came to believe that a Power greater than ourselves could restore us to sanity.<br /> 3. Made a decision to turn our will and our lives over to the care of God as we understood Him.<br /> 4. Made a searching and fearless moral inventory of ourselves.<br /> 5. Admitted to God, to ourselves, and to another human being the exact nature of our wrongs.<br /> 6. Were entirely ready to have God remove all these defects of character.<br /> 7. Humbly asked Him to remove our shortcomings.<br /> 8. Made a list of all persons we had harmed, and became willing to make amends to them all.<br /> 9. Made direct amends to such people wherever possible, except when to do so would injure them or others.<br /> 10. Continued to take personal inventory and when we were wrong promptly admitted it.<br /> 11. Sought through prayer and meditation to improve our conscious contact with God as we understood Him, praying only for knowledge of His will for us and the power to carry that out.<br /> 12. Having had a spiritual awakening as the result of these steps, we tried to carry this message to others, and to practice these principles in all our affairs.<br /> <br /> Here &quot;Power greater than ourselves&quot; is not alluding to just the God of Christianity it is suppose to accommodate people of different faiths<br /> <br /> When I take the above and compare it to this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499461#post1499461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah. I read your assessment and went &quot;Yep, that's why the Forsworn is the Priest-they know humanity and it's secret ordering better than anyone else, and their evangelism hammers down on proud nails and boxes ill-matching pairs on the grounds of preconceptions that are easier to prop up than to remove in the name of better, filler understanding.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Priest knows the plan for you. You just have to follow it.<br /> More importantly, The Priest who knows everything about people, and the hows and whys they are, has no reason to doubt themselves. They'll tell you they always knew their reflection showed themselves. They know the plan for themselves.<br /> <br /> Pay no attention to the toothy smirk in the mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just clashes, that is the stereotypical look at religious figures, the caricature of them, this only happens when the Priest is only a facade for what the character actually is.<br /> <br /> I guess that what I'm trying to get at is, what is or what do you call the character under the mask?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T20:20:43-08:00","id":1499717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499714#post1499714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sorry but the more you explain to me the character of the Forsworn the less I see the name Priest/Sacrosanct as fitting-</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but my overall goal was trying to help you grok what rejection of fear of the other meaningfully looks like in the context of this game and the hack goal first, so before we get back into the name, did that help you understand that somewhat better?<br /> <br /> I have my own thoughts on the rest of the takeaway, but Order of Operations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T22:41:32-08:00","id":1499721,"title":"","content":"Still not the full response to the recent But What ABout Hero Trend, because busy/also gotta sleep, but a related point on it:<br /> <br /> Being the person who has a general stance <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=822158#post822158\">that monstrosity is not an insurmountable impediment to being dedicated to altruism</a> and strongly emphasizes <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1394516-the-humanity-of-beast-the-primordial#post1394516\">the franchise's overall use of monstrosity as a lens on humanity</a>, I think it's safe to say that my response to people who want to explore a lower-haitch heroism for their investment in it as iconography for altruistic action is going to be &quot;Then play a fucking hero, you don't need Heroes for that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast is a game that critically examines and ultimately criticizes the heroic ideal and it's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q9zR4lWyVN8\" target=\"_blank\">most infamously adjoined</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ET4BJIdZKa0\" target=\"_blank\">partner in crime</a>. Here, we're looking at heroes-as-monsters. Surprising no one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-15-2022, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T23:55:59-08:00","id":1499725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499702#post1499702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll address the rest later, but some quick response before getting back to work:<br /> <br /> 1) Heroic Inheritances, they're a thing of intention.<br /> 2) Fatalism is core to the horror of Beast.<br /> 3) I wouldn't neccesarily call reconciling one's psychological hang-ups and learning to embrace one's vulnerabilities and permitting one's self to feel fully &quot;just stop being a Hero, dumbass&quot;. I call it healing. It's a process.<br /> 4) Also, as a corollary, they could become Beasts.<br /> 5) But also, these are still antagonists. I'm not here to give happy endings to these guys, I'm here to make them compelling narrative foils and scene-setters.<br /> 6) Also, you missed the worst of outcomes for them- <i>they win</i>. <i>They never stop winning</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright.<br /> <br /> 1) Are &quot;Heroic Inheritances&quot; in the Beast Player's Guide, I assume? Or are you hinting towards an idea that is not official material but could exist in some way?<br /> <br /> 2) No arguments against this, you are simply correct.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm probably biased and ill-equipped to understand the healing process, what with being a pathological grudge-bearer and copium-addict. That being said, it might be illustrative to see an essay about how the Forsworn lead their lives after overcoming Heroism, but maybe that wouldn't be as interesting as I am imagining. I might give it a shot, who knows.<br /> <br /> 4) I don't understand. You can experience the Devouring after the Conquering?<br /> <br /> 5) I admit my initial phrasing probably sounded like I wanted a free lunch, but I don't. I wasn't strictly inquiring about any sort of permanent cathartic transcendence, just some options for sidegrades rather than upgrades or downgrades, so to say. But maybe that's already there? I am unsure. I idly pondered the idea of a Persistent Condition or Heroic Gift only available to Heroes with a reasonably high Integrity or who uphold some ethical code based on their Life, but that's not really transcendence either, more like mitigation of the worst incentives and rewards.<br /> <br /> 6) Funny you should mention this. I'm working on a strictly antagonistic Hero who did exactly that: he just kept winning, and he's not happy about it, but doesn't know how to stop. I might post him in the forums later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499708#post1499708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that Heroes were before the signal-to-noise ratio went to shit was never about being a mythic archetype. Antagonist Heroes are built having crossed the threshold of &quot;resemblance to the mythic/folkloric basis of your supernatural creature-type is overwhelmingly a failstate.&quot; Temenotic Dreamborn are bad news as actors on the worldly stage \u2014 even the people possessed by <i>their own reputation</i> don't get out of it in a good state of being. There's a reason the least-condemned &quot;unite yourself with a supernatural force&quot; outcome in the setting is the one that preserves your individuality by being a route to Ascension rather than literally anything trucking with ephemeral/invisible entities.<br /> <br /> There is a real extent to which this question is as flawed as &quot;can a Ridden find fulfillment and purpose by assembling a different spirit to possess them, or are their options limited to dying in a conflict with werewolves or stopping being Ridden?&quot;<br /> <br /> Even without accounting for the fact that the Oracular state Heroism derived from wasn't so far gone as to need a Life connecting them to mundane context, the Forsworn have committed to a cycle of violence wherein they seize Primordial power through the most overt form of power-claim there is. The Heroic cycle is literally ritualized murder to seize worldly power through your placement as a fulcrum for the unconscious power of collective humanity in reaction to the intrusion of the monstrous into that metaphorical space. The rest is decoration upon that line.<br /> <br /> <i>Chop water, carry wood.</i> The ideal version of that role is &quot;<a href=\"https://worsethanmanyfairies.tumblr.com/post/156325762815\" target=\"_blank\">Become a good person. That is all.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a reason the supernatural beings most associated with power constrained by morality and ideals are also notorious for adhering to codes of honor impossible for mortal souls to keep. This is a universe where Mummy's metaphysic presents one of the broadest applicable views around \u2014 the Law's a bastard, and humanity was create to trip over it often enough to feed the cosmic Devil in its service. You can be a good person who has magic powers, but that's generally &quot;in spite of,&quot; not &quot;thanks to.&quot;<br /> <br /> That midpoint is &quot;magic is not a toy, lay off the sauce, the real power is the friends you make along the way.&quot; The Self is a deep road with many turnings, <i>and most of them are bad places to commit to</i>.<br /> <br /> The general process of getting the Astral to listen to you entails Inheritance and/or knowing how to manipulate people and narrative, and both of those involve a fair bit of power (which, for Heroes, probably also entails murder, because there is no store-bought Primordial power short of getting entangled with Beasts in their own pursuits). Having the sway to convince thousands of people up is down is pretty much just normal fame and persuasion, with all the upkeep that entails if you're not bringing magical backing into the equation. This is not a route to power that doesn't look bastardous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll summarize because I'm struggling to parse a lot of what you said. You're a genuinely intelligent and observant person, but your constant usage of vaguely-delineated and quasi-poetic wording often makes your intent rather opaque and difficult to discern. Not in a way that seems malicious, but it feels like you sometimes use too much energy to select more evocative words when simpler words would work better. Anyway, to summarize. I am aware that the Astral is not an exception to the over-arching theme of supernatural power coming at a price and &quot;gravitating&quot; towards individuals who are willing and even eager to cause horrific harm to become powerful.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking for Princess: The Hopeful or Paragon: The Questing or anything like that, just to be more clear. I just believe it'd be neat to populate the Bright Dream with more entities, items, areas and plot hooks to make it as fleshed out as the Primordial Dream is currently. I don't subscribe to the model of Bright = Good and Primordial = Evil. Perhaps I constrained myself in a misleading way by phrasing it as &quot;alternate types of Heroes, but genuinely heroic&quot;. Let me correct that. How about we get distinct roles/archetypes for the Bright Dream's chosen ones (or doomed ones, more likely)? As an example: The Fool As Monster. A repeating mythic / psycho-spiritual pattern that can lead people to become Fool-like personas in the Monomyth, but their major malfunction is not a violent impulse, it's more like a compulsive need to experience and promote laughter as a remedy against fear. Surely this can lead to toxic and unhinged coping mechanisms analogously to Heroes in the Forsworn model.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499721#post1499721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still not the full response to the recent But What ABout Hero Trend, because busy/also gotta sleep, but a related point on it:<br /> <br /> Being the person who has a general stance <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero?p=822158#post822158\">that monstrosity is not an insurmountable impediment to being dedicated to altruism</a> and strongly emphasizes <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1394516-the-humanity-of-beast-the-primordial#post1394516\">the franchise's overall use of monstrosity as a lens on humanity</a>, I think it's safe to say that my response to people who want to explore a lower-haitch heroism for their investment in it as iconography for altruistic action is going to be &quot;Then play a fucking hero, you don't need Heroes for that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast is a game that critically examines and ultimately criticizes the heroic ideal and it's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q9zR4lWyVN8\" target=\"_blank\">most infamously adjoined</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ET4BJIdZKa0\" target=\"_blank\">partner in crime</a>. Here, we're looking at heroes-as-monsters. Surprising no one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I genuinely cannot parse this, it feels contradictory to me. If monstrosity is not an impediment to altruism, and Heroes are a type of monster, then surely they too can be altruistic in spite of their monstrous natures? Or am I to believe only Beasts really count for such purposes because [Reasons]? And while it is completely true I do not inherently need Heroes to roleplay heroic fantasies, I'd be happy if it was acknowledged as a valid play-style and a bit of support was offered.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't want Heroes to be squeaky-clean, goody two shoes, cardboard-flavored noodles. That's no fun either. I know that Beast criticizes the Heroic ideal, but surely a few people get closer to embodying this ideal than others? As for the videos you linked... I don't have the energy or goodwill to watch and ponder that kind of analysis anymore. And I'd rather not unpack the reasons for such unwillingness, sorry. But suffice to say I do not believe a viewership-driven complex of such magnitude is a productive platform for genuine discussion anymore, sociopolitical leanings be damned. I much prefer to have direct dialogues, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-15-2022, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T03:57:28-08:00","id":1499735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499717#post1499717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but my overall goal was trying to help you grok what rejection of fear of the other meaningfully looks like in the context of this game and the hack goal first, so before we get back into the name, did that help you understand that somewhat better?<br /> <br /> I have my own thoughts on the rest of the takeaway, but Order of Operations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah I think I have a better idea of the whole thing for the rejection of the fear of the other, still don't see how it clicks with the Priest name, it feels like you are telling me to look right, while pointing left then I'm left confused with the whole thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T04:00:17-08:00","id":1499736,"title":"","content":"I'm writing at work so I must be brief, but I have two observations:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I like the term &quot;Priest&quot; for Inguma Forsworn, but I have a hypothesis on why others can't connect with it. This monicker makes sense when you look at a Priest's relationship with their community. Someone who draws lines in the sand between acceptable an unacceptable, and advocates for them. That term becomes more confused if instead, you look at their relationship with their ideal. Perhaps, &quot;Sacrosanct&quot; really is a better term, since it implies a certain attitude these Heroes would cultivate in themselves and others. It gets into the Hero's head, rather that describing their public image.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Due to developer's incompetence, the Beast Corebook had a tone of hipocrisy, when treated as a consistent whole. To avoid the same pitfall in the future, I am certain that Heroes and Beasts must be treated as equal opposites across an amoral line. If Beasts can try to learn about their blind spots and grow as people, trying to make the best of their condition, then Heroes must have the same option. The fact that Heroes who attempt this would play into their reputation as &quot;good guys&quot; would be incidental, but not the writing goal. The communication issue we're experiencing stems from the fact that &quot;What about heroic Heroes? They should all be this way&quot; and &quot;What about heroic Heroes? Some should succeed in being that&quot; are easy to mistake with one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T04:28:47-08:00","id":1499737,"title":"","content":"Seconding \u201cthe Sacrosanct\u201d, even though my line of reasoning is a lot flimsier: it sounds cool enough as a self-proclaimed title, and yet ominous enough as an adverserial one. (Hey, we\u2019ve gotta compete with things like the Victorious or the Immortal)<br /> <br /> For the good-ish Heroes: we could borrow some concepts from Guardians/Nemeses from Deviant. Balancing Legend and Life, mirroring the balance of Conviction and Loyalty. It also mirrors the Incarnate Inheritance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T05:34:28-08:00","id":1499739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499725#post1499725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll summarize because I'm struggling to parse a lot of what you said. You're a genuinely intelligent and observant person, but your constant usage of vaguely-delineated and quasi-poetic wording often makes your intent rather opaque and difficult to discern. Not in a way that seems malicious, but it feels like you sometimes use too much energy to select more evocative words when simpler words would work better.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/13.7/2014/02/03/270680304/this-could-have-been-shorter\" target=\"_blank\">You've got that backwards,</a> but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit?p=1187705#post1187705\">moving on</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps I constrained myself in a misleading way by phrasing it as &quot;alternate types of Heroes, but genuinely heroic&quot;. Let me correct that. How about we get distinct roles/archetypes for the Bright Dream's chosen ones (or doomed ones, more likely)? As an example: The Fool As Monster. A repeating mythic / psycho-spiritual pattern that can lead people to become Fool-like personas in the Monomyth, but their major malfunction is not a violent impulse, it's more like a compulsive need to experience and promote laughter as a remedy against fear. Surely this can lead to toxic and unhinged coping mechanisms analogously to Heroes in the Forsworn model. </div> </div> </div>You have missed the other point I had been making, which I had stated through fairly explicit comparison: Heroes aren't meant to be embodying Astral archetypes.<br /> <br /> The Dark Eras material describing what they were like before the world changed to interfere with their ability to be a semi-healthy response to the Begotten had them acting <i>less</i> like people bound to a role, and outside of the specific metaphysical context of Heroism that condition is generally called <i>being possessed.</i> There's horror in that, to be sure, but it doesn't have anything to do with the response of human culture to supernaturally-backed fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T06:00:20-08:00","id":1499742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499739#post1499739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.npr.org/sections/13.7/2014/02/03/270680304/this-could-have-been-shorter\" target=\"_blank\">You've got that backwards,</a> but <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit?p=1187705#post1187705\">moving on</a>.<br /> <br /> You have missed the other point I had been making, which I had stated through fairly explicit comparison: Heroes aren't meant to be embodying Astral archetypes.<br /> <br /> The Dark Eras material describing what they were like before the world changed to interfere with their ability to be a semi-healthy response to the Begotten had them acting <i>less</i> like people bound to a role, and outside of the specific metaphysical context of Heroism that condition is generally called <i>being possessed.</i> There's horror in that, to be sure, but it doesn't have anything to do with the response of human culture to supernaturally-backed fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never knew your particular style of wording came from that sort of thing. I don't think I was anywhere near as gratuitously snarky as that other fella you responded to, but even so, I did assume deliberation to sound smart on your part, and I apologize for that. I'll keep it mind from now on, and will ask for clarifications if need be.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;embody&quot;, I was not necessarily meaning something like &quot;being supernaturally compelled by Goetia&quot;. I meant more in the symbolic sense. I'm having difficulty finding the correct way to explain myself in a way that won't accidentally miss your points again, and I do not wish to frustrate you, so perhaps that is a sign for me to pause my engagement with this thread for now. Have a good day, Satchel.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T07:11:52-08:00","id":1499748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499736#post1499736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm writing at work so I must be brief, but I have two observations:<br /> <br /> \u2022 I like the term &quot;Priest&quot; for Inguma Forsworn, but I have a hypothesis on why others can't connect with it. This monicker makes sense when you look at a Priest's relationship with their community. Someone who draws lines in the sand between acceptable an unacceptable, and advocates for them. That term becomes more confused if instead, you look at their relationship with their ideal. Perhaps, &quot;Sacrosanct&quot; really is a better term, since it implies a certain attitude these Heroes would cultivate in themselves and others. It gets into the Hero's head, rather that describing their public image.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be it, not sure if it hits the issue in the head but it feels like it comes really close, the problem with the whole thing for myself is that I can't divest the ideal from the Priest as a character, the moment you take away that...let's call it core or essence of the character you turn it into something else, I struggle getting my point across but I'll try again using another set of examples of characters dealing with the role of a Priest, and I make the distinction with the capital letter to characters wearing the guise of a priest (as in the badges of office, the temple, the symbols), take a look at both Gandalf and Saruman from the Lord of the Rings, they are both wizards, both do magic, now try to sell on me on the idea that they are the same type of character and my brain is going to blue screen trying to work that out.<br /> <br /> In many ways Gandalf takes the role of the Priest of the party as a spiritual guide for the heroes, he grows into his role during the story, Saruman on the other hand does his best to remove himself away from that role, turning into something else during the progression of story, going back to the example of Javert, I'm not sure if I remember reading it but at least in one of the interpretation of the character he's seen trying to take on the role of the Priest when talking to Fantine a few times, he fails because he's a fanatic and a tyrant with the law, and if I understood it right, he's the Forsworn of The Other because he fails to understand Fantine circumstances and what led to her state and decisions blinded by his own perspective of how the world and people work.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T11:40:22-08:00","id":1499771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499725#post1499725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I genuinely cannot parse this, it feels contradictory to me. If monstrosity is not an impediment to altruism, and Heroes are a type of monster, then surely they too can be altruistic in spite of their monstrous natures? Or am I to believe only Beasts really count for such purposes because [Reasons]? And while it is completely true I do not inherently need Heroes to roleplay heroic fantasies, I'd be happy if it was acknowledged as a valid play-style and a bit of support was offered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453887#post1453887\">gone on record</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1455167-the-namtaru-and-the-immortal?p=1455171#post1455171\">several times</a> that Beast would <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1449109-so-i-ve-read-some-reviews?p=1451413#post1451413\">be a boring game</a> if either Beasts or Heroes were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious?p=1452407#post1452407\">morally all in the right</a> all the time, and have made it clear that I consider successful design of the conflict between the two stems from the fact that both start from the same dark gray moral line. That focus, however, does not change the fact that a defining characteristic of Heroes is that, whatever the reason, their method of opposition is heavily reliant on killing Beasts. the act being justified not needing to factor into it. There's no particular way this ends as a good look, and I don't particularly feel any debt or interest in trying to make it otherwise. There are games to explore and celebrate heroism as the iconogrpahy of altruism. This game is not it, and I will not make it try to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T13:04:59-08:00","id":1499780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499771#post1499771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453887#post1453887\">gone on record</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1455167-the-namtaru-and-the-immortal?p=1455171#post1455171\">several times</a> that Beast would <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1449109-so-i-ve-read-some-reviews?p=1451413#post1451413\">be a boring game</a> if either Beasts or Heroes were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious?p=1452407#post1452407\">morally all in the right</a> all the time, and have made it clear that I consider successful design of the conflict between the two stems from the fact that both start from the same dark gray moral line. That focus, however, does not change the fact that a defining characteristic of Heroes is that, whatever the reason, their method of opposition is heavily reliant on killing Beasts. the act being justified not needing to factor into it. There's no particular way this ends as a good look, and I don't particularly feel any debt or interest in trying to make it otherwise. There are games to explore and celebrate heroism as the iconogrpahy of altruism. This game is not it, and I will not make it try to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not know what you mean when you say &quot;no particular way this ends as a good look&quot;. I do want to make it totally clear that I was not trying to make you feel indebted to make changes solely for my sake, as I already pointed out quite explicitly. In fact, I admire your tenacity and focus in keeping your preferred type of thematic cohesiveness and clarity. I'll just do what I always have, and write my own Chronicles to fit my sensibilities. I hear your intent loud and clear, and will adjust my expectations accordingly. Have a good day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T17:02:12-08:00","id":1499797,"title":"","content":"So to properly address the general &quot;If you value the moral equivalence of Beasts and Heroes, why Heroes written way they are?&quot;:<br /> <br /> So I feel like it might be useful to return to the beginning of the Forsworn Heroes and the whys of it all to address this.<br /> <br /> Back in 2019, when I was riding high on life before crashing and burning, and the idea that Cinder and I should try and claim Developer-hood over Beast was a very vibrant dream, we sat down and had a quick figuring of what were actual things that really needed retooling with Beast. The first and most obvious answer was &quot;Something had to be done about Heroes&quot;, followed by &quot;THe Astral/Dreaming needs to factor more into the gameplay and setting of Beast&quot;. In defining what had to be particularly addressed with Heroes, the priorities were to make a clear, understandable, and simple point to anchor Heroes on that would handily answer &quot;What's with the beef between Beasts and Heroes?&quot;, and to find a way to empower them without neccesarily making them stronger than Beasts. Some ancilliary goals to that was to balance Beasts and Heroes on the same relative moral bar, and to find ways to increase Heroes viability as a crossover antagonist in the same way Beasts could function.<br /> <br /> The idea of Forsworn, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1451877-test-case-the-anakim-and-the-victorious?p=1451935#post1451935\">that Heroes were Children who Conquered their Horror rather than embracing it</a>, was a handy answer to all of those concerns, and gave some added benefits. By framing Beasts as having embraced their fear while Heroes rejected them, we have a really simple opposition that informs action and stories that grow from that core point organically and makes sense. Since in many ways it is a very personal matter of approach to things, and is supported by both character types having the Same Hunger and General Drive to Build Their Lair, it also let us properly frame them both as sitting on a dark grey line of morality as a baseline with room to be so much (and &quot;so much&quot;) better or worse from there, with Heroes having a benefit where the things they nominally represent being, on the surface, much more preferable in the broader social context to Beasts. The need to satitate Hunger seperate from building Lair also gives us a thing for Heroes to do when Beasts aren't around and a means to function as an antagonist in crossovers without losing their central importance to Beasts. The inclusion of Lair and Satiety and the metaphysical consequences that could be spun out from their rejection of fear provided a lot of design space for Hero's powers to built upon and shaped how we need them to be. Some of the other benefits included helping to draw Beast as a psychological horror game into focus, and rooting it's urban mythology genre elements into a symbol set and structure for personal conflicts and journey of discovery, healing , being overwhelmed by one's own mind, and with that making clear Beasts freedom to become active actors in that mythology while still permitting them to happily shit all over it, and allowing for the game to springboard that psychological discussion into broader sociological themes and concerns and then sew those back into the personal conflict, thus allowing us to root the game's overall criticism of heroism and monomythically-related issues as a concept into much more real and tangible terms for the audience to engage with.<br /> <br /> Notice, though, that nowhere in the priorities or the spun out benefits, does it entail that being a Hero is a <i>good </i>thing, or that it's <i>psychologically healthy</i> to be.<br /> <br /> Because it's not.<br /> <br /> A Hero could be lucky and dedicated enough to have a long life of altruism and being legitimately better than every Beast they killed, and at the end of their life they would still be discontent, miserable, and rooted in hostility-and most Heroes are not going to be that lucky or that dedicated. Being a Hero is a <i>problem.</i><br /> <br /> Beast is a psychological horror game that uses mythology for the structure, iconography, and language for exploring and expressing it's horror, themes, and ideas, and it has always anchored Heroes as antagonists on the ground there is a quintessential need for violence against Beasts as the marker and maker of that Heroism. In this view, what Beasts do, whatever else is flawed and disturbing about them, is psychologically healthy-they embrace their fears and hungers and are accountable to and for them, they are self-permissive of being lesser, of being vulnerable, sensitive, uninfluential, limited, in over their heads, and even just being afraid, and they understand their peers in life first and foremost as people like unto them. Heroes feel compelled to violence this, regardless of what the person who starts from this place is otherwise doing.<br /> <br /> The Forsworn model only essentially clarifies and solidifies the how and why it is by putting up a dichotomy of embracing fear as the starting point to a journey to a psychologically fuller and healthier position by contrasting it with a need to conquer one's fears, a position that is fundamentally impossible and toxic to try and maintain, no matter how heroic &quot;conquering your fears&quot; sounds-but that's the problem, that's almost quinessentially the heroic ideal. The reason Heroes kill Beasts is because Beasts represent everything that mindset rejects, and for whatever good emerges from that rejection (again, a subject we do want plain face, because we want work our way past the more boring and superficial conversations about morality and dig into the meat and bones of humanity and the hows and whys of people), Heroes still have a fundamental disconnect that encourages thinking of the world and others in ways that are constrained by a need to be strong, a need to always have the answer, a need to always be right, a need to be exemplary, to be the conqueror of fear, to be <i>heroic</i>, and if the world doesn't need heroes, then they'll remake the world so it does. They've traded bravery for fearlessness because, to them, to be afraid in the first place is to be lesser than what they want to be.<br /> <br /> And, like, it's understandable. Being afraid is a scary place, it's not pleasant or fun. There's a lot of shame that is thrown on being afraid. there's an assumption of inactivity when you could, instead, find the enemies that are making you afraid and instead get mad at them. Uncertainty that emerges from fear can be unsatisfying, and many people will take an answer against that uncertainty over contemplation and acceptance of no easy answer. There's a lot of personally relatable reasons why one would go that route.<br /> <br /> But at the end of the day, that's bullshit. That's always going to be bullshit. It doesn't matter how pretty the image that comes from that is, at it's core it's fundamentally flawed and rotten. But boy oh boy, doesn't it look nice.<br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, I don't owe or have interest in providing a happy ending to Heroes for <i>being</i> Heroes. I do owe them the chance to heal-they can always go and pull the Anathema from the Horror, tend to it's wounds while bearing it's thrashing lashes and offer comfort to it's pain, and with time and healing come to embrace and devour them and be embraced and devoured by them to become Beasts.<br /> <br /> But I don't owe Heroes peace or harmony or closure for being Heroes. It is a psychologically pained state that, in ignoring it's fundamental need, is going to encourage actions that control, hedge, and define, that will inevitably assume hostility. I don't promise that they'll do any good or amount to anything-though, like with Beasts, I do imply it, and more readily don't deny it (we're not Genius First Edition). They get that it's an understandable problem. They get that sometimes they'll reveal good things to consider and be-Beast is a game on the whole that points out that crooked sticks can still draw straight lines. But they don't get to have a good head space. They don't get to not be the opposition. They don't get to avoid their consequences.<br /> <br /> They get to be <i>heroic</i>.<br /> <br /> So with that said<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499701#post1499701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;99&quot;]<br /> 1) Are the Forsworn the only plot-relevant type of Hero? Beast Core had that downer of a sidebar, you know the one. &quot;Good Heroes exist but don't really matter because they are not proper antagonist material&quot;, was my takeaway from it. I am well aware we did get more nuanced Heroes in supplements, I appreciate that (especially Soccer Mom Gigachad and Tinnitus Black Manta, I might actually use them as NPCs!).<br /> <br /> 2) If there are other types which are plot-relevant, are they actually Heroes as such? Or are they distinct archetypes, with their own metaphysical niches and traits? I vaguely remember <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/571472-navio-de-tolos-beast-hunters\"><b>a thread that talked about such alternate archetypes, such as The Fool</b></a>.<br /> <br /> 3) Can Heroes change into other mythic archetypes? Does a Hero's Journey have to end in either doom/death or giving up the sword to plant flowers, or can they find fulfilment and purpose by adopting other roles, perhaps by mixing and matching ideas and symbols from the Bright Dream, Primordial Dream, and other Temenotic Realms? I wholeheartedly believe there is genuine material to explore in the idea of people who are sick of pseudo-Heroism, and want to live up to the ideal version of that role.<br /> <br /> And perhaps for a chosen few, the Astral listens and becomes psycho-spiritually linked to these individuals. Not quite Comic Book Superheroes as we see in Marvel, DC or various animes/mangas, though. Something that is a mid-point between &quot;glorious shining paragon of humanity fighting back the forces of darkness and inspiring others towards greatness&quot; and &quot;broken empty shell of an idealist who somehow has not locked themselves up and cried until they drowned in their own tears&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I've toyed around with a different take of the original empowered victim from before the final version of Beast, without any of the victim blaming and a general vibe of them being used to say &quot;Oh boy, you done fucked up&quot; with a clear narrative expectation that you're not supposed to <i>win</i> against them, just <i>survive</i> them, as well as people who get empowered as leaders in cases of disasters and can generally direct Beasts and Heroes, and a &quot;true hero&quot;. Dunno if I'd ever actually make any of them, but I've thought them.<br /> 2) I wouldn't name any of them Heroes, though, or have them have anything to do with Heroic metaphysics. The middle one is more likely to get called Luden, and the true hero, much like the tao, that is named is not the true hero. If I ever put a 'true hero' into the game, I want it to at least be a decade before people realize that was the case, and they certainly wouldn't call themselves that.<br /> 3) Inheritances, including the one where they become a Beast or otherwise just become human, are the best you get as the subject goes-and as noted, anything that goes deeper into heroism is either going to be, openly or secretly, a dive into more miserable states. Even a &quot;superhero&quot; who has won the &quot;game&quot; has only successfully quieted the part of them that's still screaming.<br /> <br /> Forsworn Heroes stabbed their id-shadow and covered it with a rug of their superego-persona. There's no amount of kittens you can pull out of trees that will actually address that problem, but on the plus side, that problem does not prohibit you from pulling kittens out of trees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-15-2022, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T19:33:35-08:00","id":1499826,"title":"","content":"I should note that, when it comes to any actual promise, while stuff like this is useful to know for the writing, that's not to say that the final product with be so sharp with any or all of these points. It informs it, but it's not the final text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T00:30:30-08:00","id":1499843,"title":"","content":"I'm writing from work... <i>again</i>, so I'll make my questions brief.<br /> <br /> \u2022 How do you feel about the following bit of nuance: An Enlightened Forsworn has a rabid hatred for all who do their monstrous work in secrecy, for the affront it causes for people's right to know. Naturally, that covers the Eshmaki and miscellaneous monsters, but also mundane criminals who use information warfare to hide their tracks. However, that Hero can't find it in him to get angry at Beasts who are upfront about what they are. So, when facing with a Namtaru who manifests as a Horror to spread unpleasant revelations, the Hero finds himself approving.<br /> <br /> \u2022 How would you depict a Horror as an integral part of a proto-Beast's psyche? If mutilating a Horror is meant to be treated as unhealthy, it's important that the text doesn't treat is as an external invader. This makes me think how Beasts are often described as an Astral analogue of Sin-Eaters, and how that analogy always sat wrong with me, since the Geist was always the other, and remains so even after the Bargain (until synergy hits 10). How are proto-Beats different from mundane people?<br /> <br /> \u2022 A point related to the previous one. Do people who become Beasts know they will end up spreading fear as they accept the Devouring? Your essays seem to make no distinction between accepting that fear is a necessary thing to experience, and accepting it as a necessary thing to spread. Could such people decide that neither fusing with nor killing their Horror is the right thing to do?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Finally, how much thought did you offer to the final text? Are you still within the brainstorming stage? It would be a pity to come up with good ideas and the right tone, only to fail to transfer them to the final product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T00:45:11-08:00","id":1499845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499843#post1499843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm writing from work... <i>again</i>, so I'll make my questions brief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof. The only time I had late shifts comparable to this was as a security guard, and that was not a great time in my life. You have my sympathies<br /> <br /> I'll answer when I can, but I have a bit of a weekend coming up, so I hope I can be pre-emptively forgiven for not getting to the questions immediately. They're all really good questions, I want to answer them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T01:10:15-08:00","id":1499846,"title":"","content":"Oh, you don't have to worry. I'm actually in Europe, so I'm having eminently reasonable hours. Not all CofD fans are from the US or Brazil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T01:16:05-08:00","id":1499847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499846#post1499846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you don't have to worry. I'm actually in Europe, so I'm having eminently reasonable hours. Not all CofD fans are from the US or Brazil.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I know, and yet I admit I'm surprised.<br /> <br /> Well, all the same, I do apologize for keeping up the engagement at work. I know what a pain that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T08:18:10-08:00","id":1499856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499846#post1499846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, you don't have to worry. I'm actually in Europe, so I'm having eminently reasonable hours. Not all CofD fans are from the US or Brazil.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499846#post1499846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or Brazil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel so seen!<br /> <br /> Which is actually a big problem, because I don't want people to turn into stone.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T11:27:15-08:00","id":1500058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1499843#post1499843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm writing from work... <i>again</i>, so I'll make my questions brief.<br /> <br /> \u2022 How do you feel about the following bit of nuance: An Enlightened Forsworn has a rabid hatred for all who do their monstrous work in secrecy, for the affront it causes for people's right to know. Naturally, that covers the Eshmaki and miscellaneous monsters, but also mundane criminals who use information warfare to hide their tracks. However, that Hero can't find it in him to get angry at Beasts who are upfront about what they are. So, when facing with a Namtaru who manifests as a Horror to spread unpleasant revelations, the Hero finds himself approving.<br /> <br /> \u2022 How would you depict a Horror as an integral part of a proto-Beast's psyche? If mutilating a Horror is meant to be treated as unhealthy, it's important that the text doesn't treat is as an external invader. This makes me think how Beasts are often described as an Astral analogue of Sin-Eaters, and how that analogy always sat wrong with me, since the Geist was always the other, and remains so even after the Bargain (until synergy hits 10). How are proto-Beats different from mundane people?<br /> <br /> \u2022 A point related to the previous one. Do people who become Beasts know they will end up spreading fear as they accept the Devouring? Your essays seem to make no distinction between accepting that fear is a necessary thing to experience, and accepting it as a necessary thing to spread. Could such people decide that neither fusing with nor killing their Horror is the right thing to do?<br /> <br /> \u2022 Finally, how much thought did you offer to the final text? Are you still within the brainstorming stage? It would be a pity to come up with good ideas and the right tone, only to fail to transfer them to the final product.</div> </div> </div> </div>So.<br /> <br /> 1) Oh yeah, I definitely grok that, and it's part of the reason why a) the final text, while not going to ignore the thesis about psychological health, isn't going to lean hard into it, and more importantly b) we sort of ignore the versimilitude of connection between psychological health and moral action. There's a good space for character drama and narrative opportun ties by letting the two play against each other, and as a simpler version of the proposed, I think there's a lot of interest in situations where a Hero shows up because the player Beast group is <i>of course</i> the problem but finds they can't actually against them because <i>just look at what they're doing</i> (in a good sense). The tension between what a Hero thinks about what Beasts are versus what a Beast actually <i>does</i> is one with a lot of forms for fun conflict and thoughtful narrative.<br /> <br /> 2) While I enjoyed it the first time it got emphasized in the BPG, I've since cooled on the &quot;Horror-as-Seperate-and-Equal-Partner-in-a-Beast&quot;. It does tread into Geist territory, it leans towards a lot of takes i've seen that go &quot;Beast've been better if Beasts were prisons and binders of legendary monsters who have to tragically struggle against what that does to them&quot; that I generally despise, and on the whole I don't think it actually serves Beast all that well, particularly when so much of the game makes more sense on the psychological level then not, and should lean more into it. Becoming a Beast is still a <i>choice</i>, but it should be clear-the things that make a prospective Deep Dreamer a viable half of a future beast includes that all the pieces were already t<i>here</i>-the fear, the hunger, the feeling more people are connected to this than not, and even the self-transcendent nature of those feelings were all things the Deep Dreamer already had. The confrontation with the Horror makes it plain and graspable, and stepping into the Devouring is the fullest extent of that.<br /> <br /> Deep Dreamers are a concept I want to flesh out more as a proper Dyad and proto state for all the Children-Beasts, Heroes, and Insatiable alike. I would need to really getting around to that to get what it means, but as a base idea, beyond what's been mentioned on the idea before, I do think that all of them have a pronounced relationship with what can be called the id or the shadow before hand, in an emotional or thoughtful or spiritual awareness of some sort that allows them, in a couple of ways, dig deep into themselves and connect to the Primordial Dream. It need not always be positive, need not always lead to a acceptance of what it represents, or be either innate or practiced. I look forward to working on them more in future.<br /> <br /> 3) While the family essays haven't gone into it much, I know I've made the point more than a couple times that one of the things that makes Beast a game about accountability is the fact that the Devouring very much makes it clear what they do to others, because the Horror puts them through the exact same wringer, and it doesn't so with the thoughtfulness and consideration a later Beast might do it with, because the Horror is an animal impulse actor. On the other hand, part of the reason why we try to frame exploring and getting comfortable with fear is to make the point that Satiation as a means of confronting the self, the true shape of one's fears and anxieities, and the uses and abuses of the security practices we use to handle that, is a very viable form of action to pursue-the Beast acting as both a guide and an adversarial force in an externalized psychodrama allows for Beasts to turn Satiation for themselves into a form of mini-Devouring for the victim, even if they don't walk away with cool Dreaming Powers and the like, and in kind can allow Beasts to understand the ways they could have been their victims, and to take their particular strengths and wisdom onto themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> Or they could just be jerks, or not really have the time to get in deep with someone. As one of those &quot;Extreme position used as a knife to cut shape to the final form&quot;, we generally take game as a game of assholes being assholes to each other first, and self-determining wherther that assholery will be directed towards making the world a bit less of asshole place or to being an even bigger asshole second. While nothing is ignored or excluded, and the two are ultimately intended to be paired as equal, Transgression still has a nominal top billing ahead of Kinship, and in the same way there should always be Sleeping Beauties but there will always be Thaddeus Pearsons (and fuck that guy), there should always be Beasts who build as they eat, but there always will be Beasts who just eat.<br /> <br /> The game is a matter of balancing a lot of plates, but a lot of problems with the original core come from a failure to do that, and one of the reasons why that is, on top of all the mismanagement, is the failure to not anchor in a direction and then grow or deviate from it. Beast going forward should probably fix that by first anchoring in the bleak and then building up the positive as an equal from that afterwards. To mangle Wreck-It Ralph, you've got to be a bad guy before you can make the point that that doesn't mean you're a <i>bad guy, </i>as it were. Sometimes you really do mean to do right by the people you eat, but that doesn't mean that sometimes you just gotta punch a guy in the face for a bite so you can then burn down Musk's house.<br /> <br /> 4) Books are being written, vague plans are turning into proper outlines, notes and ideas and conversations are being consolidated, evaluated, and placed, with firm lines being drawn, somethings are actually going into the trash finally. While there's still some biding of time and holding out hope (because some things have muddied the mood that was leading to commitment), work that started in 2019 is now being crunched into products, commitments are starting to get made.<br /> <br /> The Forsworn have the theme of Familial Strife and the mood of Unsatisfying Satiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-18-2022, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-18T13:10:18-08:00","id":1500065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1499276-the-inguma-and-the-similar?p=1500058#post1500058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.<br /> <br /> 1) Oh yeah, I definitely grok that, and it's part of the reason why a) the final text, while not going to ignore the thesis abo